{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01XkaM9Z6bHd6CGFE5W7nPA1","lastSequenceNum":0,"ownerAccountUuid":"f907b165-4712-485f-a44b-7f7d54b74cf9","ownerOrganizationUuid":"77d6453f-aaee-4ad3-a7ea-34b17cbaf2e5"}
{"parentUuid":"ad9de8ae-6bd7-4fbf-af0f-d35cc1be6bbe","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cc6b4e86-18b8-4e65-826e-ac485cbab2ac","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F6fXixkJ65GArtAbcTKY9u","type":"tool_result","content":"The page is an introduction and covers only authentication, errors, and pointers to other sections. It doesn't document the payment-creation endpoint, so I can't give you a complete integration spec from it.\n\n**What the page covers**\n\n- **Base URL:** `https://app.platega.io/`\n- **Format:** JSON over HTTPS.\n- **Auth headers:** `X-MerchantId` (your store ID) and `X-Secret` (your API key). The page says the secret must not be sent to the client, which matters for a Telegram bot, since it should only call Platega from your server.\n- **Example endpoint:** `GET /transaction/{id}` appears in a curl example with both headers. The page doesn't describe its response fields or status values.\n- **Invalid key:** The API returns HTTP `401` with `code` \"Auth:GEN_1001\", `type` 4002, and message \"Access denied.\" Log the `traceId` for support.\n- **Error format:** Every error has `code`, `type` (integer), `message`, `data` (array of field-level details), and `traceId`.\n- **Payouts:** The payout API uses a different scheme: an `Authorization: PG-HMAC` header with an HMAC-SHA256 signature, and it does not use `X-MerchantId` or `X-Secret`. Details are in the \"Выводы\" section.\n- **Callbacks:** Platega sends status-change notifications as `POST` requests to your URL. The body format, URL requirements, retry behavior, and status list are in the \"Callbacks\" section.\n\n**What the page does not cover**\n\n- The endpoint to create a payment or transaction (method, path, request fields)\n- Payment method codes (SBP, cards, crypto), amount, currency, description, return/failure URLs, and payload\n- Response fields (transaction ID, redirect URL, status)\n- Callback headers for verification, body fields, and statuses such as CONFIRMED or CANCELED\n- Any test or sandbox mode\n\n**Sub-pages**\n\nThe page names two sections but gives no URLs for them: \"Выводы\" (payouts) and \"Callbacks.\" Check the Platega documentation site navigation for their addresses, or ask your Platega manager for the create-transaction and callback specs."}]},"uuid":"eb79da13-e233-4614-ad1a-fbce4b218535","timestamp":"2026-10-31T21:31:18.033Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":3170,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"The page is an introduction and covers only authentication, errors, and pointers to other sections. It doesn't document the payment-creation endpoint, so I can't give you a complete integration spec from it.\n\n**What the page covers**\n\n- **Base URL:** `https://app.platega.io/`\n- **Format:** JSON over HTTPS.\n- **Auth headers:** `X-MerchantId` (your store ID) and `X-Secret` (your API key). The page says the secret must not be sent to the client, which matters for a Telegram bot, since it should only call Platega from your server.\n- **Example endpoint:** `GET /transaction/{id}` appears in a curl example with both headers. The page doesn't describe its response fields or status values.\n- **Invalid key:** The API returns HTTP `401` with `code` \"Auth:GEN_1001\", `type` 4002, and message \"Access denied.\" Log the `traceId` for support.\n- **Error format:** Every error has `code`, `type` (integer), `message`, `data` (array of field-level details), and `traceId`.\n- **Payouts:** The payout API uses a different scheme: an `Authorization: PG-HMAC` header with an HMAC-SHA256 signature, and it does not use `X-MerchantId` or `X-Secret`. Details are in the \"Выводы\" section.\n- **Callbacks:** Platega sends status-change notifications as `POST` requests to your URL. The body format, URL requirements, retry behavior, and status list are in the \"Callbacks\" section.\n\n**What the page does not cover**\n\n- The endpoint to create a payment or transaction (method, path, request fields)\n- Payment method codes (SBP, cards, crypto), amount, currency, description, return/failure URLs, and payload\n- Response fields (transaction ID, redirect URL, status)\n- Callback headers for verification, body fields, and statuses such as CONFIRMED or CANCELED\n- Any test or sandbox mode\n\n**Sub-pages**\n\nThe page names two sections but gives no URLs for them: \"Выводы\" (payouts) and \"Callbacks.\" Check the Platega documentation site navigation for their addresses, or ask your Platega manager for the create-transaction and callback specs.","durationMs":10430,"url":"https://docs.platega.io/"},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"08f74202-7f47-4352-8d1c-0838e2d532b3","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/Sagenkazaran/Library/Application Support/Claude/scratch-workspaces/f907b165-4712-485f-a44b-7f7d54b74cf9/77d6453f-aaee-4ad3-a7ea-34b17cbaf2e5/scratch-2026-10-26-b13584","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":null,"remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]},"error":"not_a_repo"},"live_cwd":"/Users/Sagenkazaran/Library/Application Support/Claude/scratch-workspaces/f907b165-4712-485f-a44b-7f7d54b74cf9/77d6453f-aaee-4ad3-a7ea-34b17cbaf2e5/scratch-2026-10-26-b13584","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ad9de8ae-6bd7-4fbf-af0f-d35cc1be6bbe","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/Sagenkazaran/Library/Application Support/Claude/scratch-workspaces/f907b165-4712-485f-a44b-7f7d54b74cf9/77d6453f-aaee-4ad3-a7ea-34b17cbaf2e5/scratch-2026-10-26-b13584","sessionId":"1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"deep-singing-taco"}
