{"parentUuid":"d8a87863-b2aa-43dc-bdf5-372920c3c1c4","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"c07342c3-c5db-4dab-b77b-973a6227d973","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>Agent, AskUserQuestion, Bash, Edit, Read, SendUserFile, Skill, ToolSearch, WebFetch, WebSearch, Write, mcp__Claude_Browser__browser_batch, mcp__Claude_Browser__computer, mcp__Claude_Browser__find, mcp__Claude_Browser__javascript_tool, mcp__Claude_Browser__navigate, mcp__Claude_Browser__preview_start, mcp__Claude_Browser__preview_stop, mcp__Claude_Browser__resize_window, mcp__ccd_directory__request_directory, mcp__ccd_host__reveal_path, mcp__ccd_session__mark_chapter, mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan, mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up, mcp__computer-use__app_batch, mcp__computer-use__app_click, mcp__computer-use__app_list_windows, mcp__computer-use__app_release, mcp__computer-use__app_screenshot, mcp__computer-use__open_application, mcp__computer-use__request_access, mcp__kling__query_membership_and_credits, mcp__kling__who_am_i, mcp__obsidian__obsidian_edit_note, mcp__terminal__read_terminal, mcp__terminal__run_in_terminal</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n\n   **Who the user is and standing rules**\n   - The user is господин Шаген (Shahen Kazaryan, shahen.hay@live.com, GitHub Shahen777). He is non-technical and Russian-speaking, and prefers short plain-Russian answers and one decision at a time.\n   - Every reply starts with «Господин Шаген, …».\n   - Log significant work to Obsidian note `Проекты/VPN-инфраструктура.md` (vault id `vault`).\n   - Verbatim security rules:\n     - «.env, ключи API, токены и приватные документы клиентов никогда не коммитить». Check `git ls-files | grep -E '(^|/)\\.env$'`.\n     - «Логин (`entire login`) и пуш чекпойнтов на серверы Entire не выполнять без явного разрешения Шагена».\n     - \"бразилия не закрывай парольный SSH и root\".\n     - Never restart x-ui/Xray on Vienna; restarting nexo-bot and the subscription services is fine.\n     - \"тот бот не трогаем\": do not touch the old Aura bot code at /opt/aura-vpn-bot-next. Its database is shared and only additive changes were made.\n     - Payment compliance: no wording about bypassing blocks.\n     - Never enter passwords into sites. The Platega test cabinet login/password was given by the user and NOT used; the keys were entered by the user via hidden dialogs.\n\n   **Requests in this period, in order**\n   1. Karing video: logo intro; first-launch screens from the user's iPhone screenshots; server explanation recommending «Автовыбор»; Marat voice; placed in the bot.\n   2. iPhone flow: ask which App Store the user has. Russian store → Karing (recommended); other store → Happ; OneXray is the backup.\n   3. Test payments via Platega; pay button in the main menu.\n   4. Web app working without Telegram or VPN, with no login (personal link).\n   5. Make it «красивый современный»:\n      - the dark version was rejected as «слишком иишный»;\n      - the light brand-blue version was liked («Нравится»);\n      - then «нужно сделать как мобильное приложение»;\n      - then «чтобы нельзя было вверх вниз не свайпалось».\n   6. Expiry enforcement and reminders; sync between bot and web («синхронизация… после подключения»).\n   7. «сделай пока что чтобы 7 дней было бесплатно» — handled by fixing the bug that showed no-date accounts as expired. New users already get 7 days.\n   8. LATEST: «в разделе поддержка сделай чтобы поддрежка была по ссылке переход на меня» — support buttons should link directly to his Telegram @Shahen_Kazaryan.\n   9. The user postponed re-entering the Platega keys («Позже»).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n\n   **Servers and services**\n   - Vienna server `codex-aura@152.53.50.204`, key `~/.ssh/codex_aura_vps`, passwordless sudo.\n   - Nexo code in `/opt/nexo-bot` (git, owner shagen). Run git as `sudo -n git -C /opt/nexo-bot -c safe.directory=/opt/nexo-bot`.\n   - Services: `nexo-bot`, `nexo-subscription` (HTTPS :8444, EnvironmentFile `/etc/aura-vpn-bot/nexo.env`).\n   - Shared SQLite database `/opt/aura-vpn-bot-next/aura_vpn.db`; backups in `/opt/aura-vpn-bot-next/backups/`.\n\n   **Local working copy**\n   - `/private/tmp/claude-501/REDACTED/1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb/scratchpad/nexo-work`.\n   - The iCloud copy at ~/Documents/Codex/.../candidate is dataless (evicted) and unreadable.\n\n   **Deploy steps**\n   1. `COPYFILE_DISABLE=1 tar --no-xattrs -czf ../x.tgz FILES`, then scp to /tmp.\n   2. Stage in ~/nexo-staging: extract current /opt/nexo-bot plus the new files, then run tests with `/opt/nexo-bot/venv/bin/python` using `PYTHONPATH=.:tests`.\n   3. Extract into /opt/nexo-bot with `--no-same-owner`, then chown to shagen.\n   4. Commit as Claude/noreply@anthropic.com with `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`.\n   5. Restart the services.\n\n   **Tests:** `PYTHONPATH=.:tests AURA_NO_CARDS=1 AURA_DB_PATH=/tmp/x.db AURA_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://example.test AURA_VERIFY_CODE=pay python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -p \"test_*.py\"`.\n\n   **Platega API**\n   - Base `https://app.platega.io`, headers `X-MerchantId` / `X-Secret`.\n   - `POST /v2/transaction/process` (paymentDetails, description, return, failedUrl, payload, orderId, metadata.user_email, userId).\n   - `GET /transaction/{id}` and `GET /balance/all`.\n   - Callback POST is authenticated with the same headers.\n   - Callback URL: `https://152.53.50.204:8444/platega/callback` (must be set in the cabinet by the user).\n   - Keys live in nexo.env as `PLATEGA_MERCHANT_ID` / `PLATEGA_SECRET`, set via `scratchpad/set_platega_keys.py` (hidden osascript dialogs, validates with /balance/all).\n   - Currently 401 SIGN_1001 «Merchant secret key is not correct» (shared test account key rotated).\n\n   **Certificates:** lego 5 renews the IP certificate into `/etc/lego/certificates/152.53.50.204.*`. The hook `/usr/local/sbin/aura-lego-deploy` was fixed to understand `LEGO_HOOK_CERT_*`, with a fallback, and to restart both `aura-vpn-subscription` and `nexo-subscription`.\n\n   **Web accounts**\n   - Negative synthetic tg_id; `users.web_token`; cookie `nexo_cabinet`; `/c/<token>`.\n   - Merge into Telegram via a one-time `link_codes` code and `t.me/NexoConnect_bot?start=web_<code>`; `users.merged_into` keeps the old link working.\n\n   **Paid period**\n   - `users.paid_until` holds an ISO naive UTC string. NULL means unlimited (old accounts).\n   - Trial is 7 days for new accounts (`device_service.TRIAL_DAYS`).\n   - `DeviceService.sync_access` suspends devices (removed from panels, status `suspended`) and resumes them. `access.access_loop` runs every 300 s in the bot and sends reminders (`reminder_for`, `expiry_notice_for`).\n\n   **Web design**\n   - Self-hosted Unbounded + Manrope fonts (`assets/web/fonts`); brand blue #2F6BFF, navy #0B1F3A.\n   - Knot logo as parametric SVG (`knot()` from `assets/web/knot.svg`).\n   - App shell: fixed app bar, bottom tab bar (home / setup / pay / more), `data-tab` sections switched by `TAB_SCRIPT`.\n   - `body` is fixed so the window never moves; `.app` is the inner scroll container; no zoom.\n\n   **Video tooling**\n   - content-factory `build_nexo_karing.py`; ElevenLabs TTS with Marat (`vQxSi2EuaRWwBw3nn6dK`, eleven_v3) and the sound-generation API.\n   - Output `data/videos/nexo-karing/nexo-karing_FINAL_intro.mp4`.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (in nexo-work, deployed unless noted):\n\n   **catalog.py**\n   - iOS app order: karing, onexray, happ.\n   - `SWITCH = {\"ios\": {\"karing\":[(\"Запасной вариант — OneXray\",\"onexray\")], \"onexray\":[(\"‹ Вернуться к Karing\",\"karing\")], \"happ\":[(\"Запасной вариант — Karing\",\"karing\")]}}`\n   - `STORE_APP = {\"ru\":\"karing\",\"other\":\"happ\",\"unknown\":\"karing\"}`\n   - `VIDEOS = {\"ios\": {\"karing\": \"karing.mp4\"}}`\n\n   **handlers/onboarding.py**\n   - Store question `store:ru|other|unknown`; `choose_store` / `start_wizard`.\n   - Step 2 has the button «▶️ Видео: как это сделать (1 мин)» (`howto:{nonce}` → `howto_video` sends video via `navigation.send_video`).\n   - Done screen: «💳 Оплатить доступ» when unpaid, plus «🌐 Веб-кабинет».\n   - Home shows «Доступ оплачен до …».\n   - Uncommitted: support buttons now use `support_button()`.\n\n   **navigation.py**: `VIDEO_DIR`, `video_path`, `send_video` (caches file_id).\n\n   **database.py**\n   - Tables: `payments`, `link_codes`.\n   - Columns: paid_until, web_token, merged_into, reminder_for, expiry_notice_for.\n   - Functions: create_payment, set_payment_provider_id, get_payment, settle_payment (idempotent; extends from max(now, paid_until)), create_web_user, get_user_by_web_token (resolves merged_into), ensure_web_token, create_link_code, merge_web_account, users_to_notify, mark_notified, _now.\n\n   **device_service.py**\n   - `TRIAL_DAYS=7`; trial on new owner.\n   - Blocks create when expired.\n   - `_clients`, `_suspend`, `_resume` (email fallback `-r<time>`), `sync_access(tg_id=None)`.\n\n   **payments.py**\n   - Functions: enabled, paid_tariffs, tariff, _request, buyer_email, create_link(tg_id,key,return_url=None) (return_url may contain {id}), check(payment, service=None) (calls resume_access), resume_access, callback_authentic, active_until, pay_label, paid_until_text, success_text, notify (skips tg_id<=0).\n\n   **access.py**: send_notices and access_loop. **bot.py** starts access_loop.\n\n   **handlers/pay.py**\n   - `pay` (choose tariff), `buy:`, `pay_check:`, `web_cabinet` (URL button to the cabinet; screen for users without an account).\n   - Uncommitted: retry screen uses `support_button()`.\n\n   **handlers/start.py**: `/start web_<code>` → merge_web_account, then reply with a «🌐 Веб-кабинет» URL button.\n\n   **handlers/devices.py**: `suspended` status texts and a «💳 Продлить» button.\n\n   **keyboards.py**\n   - main_menu(user): Подключить; pay_label; [Мои устройства, 🌐 Веб-кабинет]; [Тарифы и документы, Помощь].\n   - docs_menu has a pay row when enabled.\n   - docs_back(pay).\n   - Uncommitted:\n     ```python\n     def support_button() -> InlineKeyboardButton:\n         import legal\n         return InlineKeyboardButton(text=\"💬 Написать в поддержку\", url=legal.SUPPORT_URL)\n     def help_menu(): InlineKeyboardMarkup([[support_button()],[back_main]])\n     ```\n\n   **legal.py**\n   - Uncommitted:\n     ```python\n     SUPPORT_URL = os.environ.get(\"AURA_SUPPORT_URL\") or f\"https://t.me/{SUPPORT_CONTACT.lstrip('@')}\"\n     ```\n   - Support text updated: removed «Проверить сервис», apps listed as «Karing, OneXray или Happ».\n   - Tariffs text: «Кнопка «💳 Оплатить доступ» — в разделе «Тарифы и документы».»\n\n   **handlers/legal.py** — uncommitted: the doc_support screen prepends `[support_button()]`.\n\n   **subscription.py**\n   - request_log middleware masks any 16+ character path segment.\n   - `POST /platega/callback` resumes access and notifies.\n   - `webapp.add_routes(app)`.\n\n   **webapp.py**: the whole web app.\n   - Routes: /app, /app/start, /c/{token}, /c/{token}/device, /c/{token}/pay, /c/{token}/telegram, /docs/{name}, /media/{name}, /web/fonts/{name}, /web/{name} (icon.png, karing-poster.jpg), /web/manifest.webmanifest.\n   - App shell: appbar(), row(), DOC_ROWS, simple(), key_pass (unlimited → «Без срока»), days_left, TAB_SCRIPT, ICONS, TABS.\n   - Uncommitted:\n     - home tile «Поддержка» → SUPPORT_URL (target _blank);\n     - DOC_ROWS first row «Написать в поддержку · Telegram · @Shahen_Kazaryan» (external);\n     - /docs/support gets a «Написать в Telegram» button.\n\n   **tests**: test_payments.py, test_webapp.py (incl. link/expiry/unlimited tests), test_access.py; test_navigation.py includes the pay router.\n\n   **Server-only changes**\n   - `/usr/local/sbin/aura-lego-deploy`, with a backup `.bak-<time>`.\n   - The live cert was replaced; the old one is kept as `*.expired-<time>`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **iCloud evicted candidate files** (Operation timed out): switched to a server copy in scratchpad/nexo-work.\n   - **Disk full (ENOSPC)**: Bash could not run, so I used the terminal tool, which refuses non-ASCII text in the command (so a glob `~/*/content-factory` was used to reach the Cyrillic path). Deleted only my own temp files plus the npm cache and unavailable simulators; 6.1 GB free.\n   - **Auto-mode classifier denials**:\n     - Launching the downloaded OneXray app was denied; I asked the user to install it from the App Store, and the OneXray video was later cancelled.\n     - Cert install and hook edit were denied until the user explicitly said «Да, разрешаю» / «Да, исправляй».\n   - **Platega key dialogs**:\n     - First attempt: empty values. Second: 401/403. The validation was improved to use /balance/all and a UUID format check, and the third attempt succeeded.\n     - Later the keys broke (shared account rotated); still pending.\n   - **Headless Chrome minimum width** (~500 px) clipped previews: used the Browser pane with mobile emulation via a local http.server preview (launch.json `nexo-web-preview`, port 8796; port 8765 belonged to another session).\n   - **Sticky header broken by `overflow-x:hidden`**: made the app bar fixed. The anchor jump pushed content under the bar: switched to `data-tab` instead of ids.\n   - **Animations paused in the background pane** left content faded: keyframes now move only, no opacity.\n   - **Video**: pointer covers on screenshots; logo seam fixed by keying the logo out of the reveal frame (`cut_logo` with threshold).\n   - **Tests**:\n     - The navigation test needed the pay router.\n     - The cookie test needed a manual Cookie header (Secure cookie over HTTP).\n     - The stuck-screen tip had to contain «App Store».\n   - **Bug**: unlimited accounts showed «Не активен» — fixed in 4bcb307.\n   - **User feedback on design**: dark design «слишком иишный» → light brand design; «сделал как сайт» → app UI; «не свайпалось» → fixed window.\n   - **Current**: two failing tests after the support change (see section 8).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - **Solved**: iPhone flow; Karing video v3 in the bot; Platega integration (code works, keys invalid now); cert expiry and hook; web app (app UI, fixed window); trial, suspend/resume, reminders; account merge (verified on production: the user's iPhone web account merged into his Telegram account, which stays unlimited); unlimited display bug.\n   - **Ongoing**: the support-link change, tests failing.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"давай сделаем краисвое видео чтобы людем понятно было в разделе добавить подписку в каринг у нас такая ситуация что основной будет какринг потому что в рф апп стор happ нету подумай что можно еще добавить кроме happ и какринг но чтобы все работала подумай хорошо еще хотел узнать можно ли для iphone сделать без приложенин а через браузер?\"\n   - \"OneXray наши правила работают?\"\n   - \"Да, добавь\"\n   - \"OneXray не сработала проверь\"\n   - \"все работает уже\"\n   - \"давай сделай OneXray как основной рекамендуется\"\n   - \"давай хорошо подумай может все таки сможешь сделать так чтобы было вебприложение не через тг ?\"\n   - \"нужно чтобы очень хорошо подумал запустил большую команду агентов чтобы понять как лучше сделать через что чтобы приложение работала удобно быз глюков как OneXray и сложный как Karing подумай как нам лучше всего сделать это\"\n   - \"хорошо давай сделаем через OneXray и Karing только сделаем чтобы людем было максимально понятно нужно сделать видео ролик подключиться к нашему папку ии аген контет фабрика и так есть все апи эвеленлабс и кие ай и сделать озвучку понятную\"\n   - \"в принцпе приложение каринг на маке такое же как на телефоне можешь сделать запиь экрана найди репазитори и сделай чтобы красиво было а потом доресуй сверху\"\n   - \"Спроси доступ снова\"\n   - \"как дела?\" / \"дальше\"\n   - \"Да, продолжай\"\n   - \"не нравиться озвучка сделай нормальную и сделай так чтобы чуть живее было\"\n   - \"голос-Марат.mp3\"\n   - \"Да, делай\" (OneXray video)\n   - \"нужно в начале добавить анимированный лого\"\n   - \"в начале добаь звук появление и сделай так чтобы лого ушло ввер справо красиво встало и чуть прозрачнее и сделай так чтобы начальный кадр было чуть быстее сделай каринг рекомендованный и сделай happ но путь вопрос спросят если айфон ап стор рф то пусть сразу делает каринг если аппстор не рф тогда happ подумай как лучше сделать и можешь сделать чтобы сразу понять какой телефон чтобы не спрашивать ?\"\n   - \"Пока не нужно\" (mini app)\n   - \"OneXray пока не надо видео\"\n   - \"Да, поставь\" (video in bot)\n   - Pasted Platega test account info (Login/Password, docs links) + \"подключи тестовую оплату\"\n   - \"еще раз покажи\" / \"еще раз не правильно вставил ID мерчанта\" / \"ок\"\n   - \"может оплату в другом разделе добавии или как правильно\"\n   - Six Karing iPhone screenshots + \"давай видео чуть переделаме видео нужно дабвить эти моменты чтобы людем понятно было что делать сделай озвучку заново и в конце где говориь выбор страны сделай так чтобы выбор сервер страны короче сделай так чтобы понятно было зачем людем менять страну это сервер и скажи что рекамендуются оставлять автовыбор\"\n   - \"Да, добавь\" (pay button in menu)\n   - \"давай сделаем так в рф тг работатет тоько с впн а чтобы люди устоновили себе впн им нужно тг а в тг они не могут зайти давай найдем решение и сделаем веб приложение по ссылке\"\n   - \"освободи ты\" / \"нади что нибудь и осободи память\"\n   - \"Да, разрешаю\" (cert) / \"Да, исправляй\" (hook)\n   - \"что дальше\"\n   - \"давай делать веб приложение сначала потом купим домен\"\n   - \"чтобы было красивео веб приложение и чтобы он так же работатла без впн и без авторизаци или минимальной авторизации\"\n   - \"нужно сделать современный крсивый дизайн приложение\" (mid-turn)\n   - \"не нравиться дизай слишком иишный сделай красивый современный дизайн\"\n   - \"Нравится\"\n   - \"да\" (expiry enforcement)\n   - \"нужно чтобы синхронизация была тг бота и веб\" (mid-turn)\n   - \"покажи ссылку\"\n   - \"нужно сделать чтобы была синхронизация между веб и тг ботом после подключения\"\n   - \"Позже\" (Platega keys)\n   - \"ты тут сделал как сайт нужно сделать как приложение дизай сделай чтобы выгледило как мобтльное приложение\"\n   - \"Есть правки сделай так чтобы нельзя было вверх вниз не свайплся\"\n   - \"сделай пока что чтобы 7 дней было бесплатно\"\n   - \"в разделе поддержка сделай чтобы поддрежка была по ссылке переход на меня\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Finish the support-link change: fix the 2 failing tests, run the full suite, deploy, log to Obsidian, report.\n   - Platega: the user must re-enter the current keys later («Позже»), using `python3 scratchpad/set_platega_keys.py` (hidden dialogs), and set the Callback URL in the cabinet.\n   - Later: buy a domain and move the web app off the Vienna VPN IP.\n   - Check cert auto-renewal around 04–05.11 (`journalctl -t aura-lego-deploy`).\n\n8. Current Work:\n\n   Implementing «поддержка по ссылке переход на меня». Edits were applied in nexo-work but NOT deployed:\n   - **legal.py**: `SUPPORT_URL` (`https://t.me/Shahen_Kazaryan`, from `AURA_SUPPORT_CONTACT=@Shahen_Kazaryan`); support text cleanup.\n   - **keyboards.py**: `support_button()` URL button; help_menu uses it.\n   - **handlers/legal.py**: the doc_support screen prepends the URL button.\n   - **handlers/onboarding.py**: the provision error screen and the stuck screen use `support_button()`; import added.\n   - **handlers/pay.py**: the retry screen uses `support_button()`.\n   - **webapp.py**:\n     - home tile «Поддержка» → SUPPORT_URL with target _blank;\n     - DOC_ROWS first row is «Написать в поддержку» with sub «Telegram · @Shahen_Kazaryan» (external);\n     - the /docs/support page has a «Написать в Telegram» button.\n\n   Running the tests gave 210 tests with 2 failures:\n   - `test_legal.LegalTextsTest.test_documents_reachable_from_main_and_help_menus` (line 47): `'doc_support' not found in {None, 'back_main'}`. The help menu now uses a URL button.\n   - `test_onboarding.OnboardingTests.test_stuck_screen_offers_support_and_way_back` (line 208): `'doc_support' not found in ['ob_qr:…', None, 'step2:…']`.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n\n   Update those two tests to assert the support URL button instead of the `doc_support` callback:\n   - test_legal: check the help menu has a button with `url == legal.SUPPORT_URL`, and that doc_support is still reachable via docs_menu.\n   - test_onboarding: check that some button on the stuck screen has the `https://t.me/` url.\n\n   Then:\n   1. Rerun the full suite.\n   2. Deploy the changed files: legal.py, keyboards.py, handlers/legal.py, handlers/onboarding.py, handlers/pay.py, webapp.py and the updated tests. Use the staging pattern, commit with Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5, and restart nexo-bot and nexo-subscription.\n   3. Log to Obsidian.\n   4. Tell the user that support buttons now open his Telegram @Shahen_Kazaryan directly. Note that in Russia t.me needs a working VPN, so web users without VPN may not be able to open it, and suggest adding a non-Telegram contact (email or phone) later.\n\n   This continues the user's latest request: \"в разделе поддержка сделай чтобы поддрежка была по ссылке переход на меня\".\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/Sagenkazaran/.claude/projects/REDACTED/1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"a4e656bc-6bef-40ce-89e8-abbdb7f384ba","timestamp":"2026-11-02T15:12:22.224Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":109,"turnIndex":128},"turnOrigin":"human","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["058eba11-474e-451c-a7c5-bf1a58379440"],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/Sagenkazaran/Library/Application Support/Claude/scratch-workspaces/f907b165-4712-485f-a44b-7f7d54b74cf9/77d6453f-aaee-4ad3-a7ea-34b17cbaf2e5/scratch-2026-10-26-b13584","sessionId":"1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"deep-singing-taco"}
{"parentUuid":"a4e656bc-6bef-40ce-89e8-abbdb7f384ba","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/Sagenkazaran/Library/Application Support/Claude/scratch-workspaces/f907b165-4712-485f-a44b-7f7d54b74cf9/77d6453f-aaee-4ad3-a7ea-34b17cbaf2e5/scratch-2026-10-26-b13584/.claude/launch.json","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/Sagenkazaran/Library/Application Support/Claude/scratch-workspaces/f907b165-4712-485f-a44b-7f7d54b74cf9/77d6453f-aaee-4ad3-a7ea-34b17cbaf2e5/scratch-2026-10-26-b13584/.claude/launch.json","content":"{\n  \"version\": \"0.0.1\",\n  \"configurations\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"nexo-web-preview\",\n      \"runtimeExecutable\": \"python3\",\n      \"runtimeArgs\": [\"-m\", \"http.server\", \"8796\", \"--bind\", \"127.0.0.1\", \"--directory\", \"/private/tmp/claude-501/REDACTED/1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb/scratchpad/web_preview\"],\n      \"port\": 8796\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","numLines":12,"startLine":1,"totalLines":12}},"displayPath":".claude/launch.json"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ad572cd1-988c-4fd6-9d96-3c98ed19cf2a","timestamp":"2026-11-02T15:12:26.124Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/Sagenkazaran/Library/Application Support/Claude/scratch-workspaces/f907b165-4712-485f-a44b-7f7d54b74cf9/77d6453f-aaee-4ad3-a7ea-34b17cbaf2e5/scratch-2026-10-26-b13584/.claude/launch.json\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t{\n2\t  \"version\": \"0.0.1\",\n3\t  \"configurations\": [\n4\t    {\n5\t      \"name\": \"nexo-web-preview\",\n6\t      \"runtimeExecutable\": \"python3\",\n7\t      \"runtimeArgs\": [\"-m\", \"http.server\", \"8796\", \"--bind\", \"127.0.0.1\", \"--directory\", \"/private/tmp/claude-501/REDACTED/1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb/scratchpad/web_preview\"],\n8\t      \"port\": 8796\n9\t    }\n10\t  ]\n11\t}\n12\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/Sagenkazaran/Library/Application Support/Claude/scratch-workspaces/f907b165-4712-485f-a44b-7f7d54b74cf9/77d6453f-aaee-4ad3-a7ea-34b17cbaf2e5/scratch-2026-10-26-b13584","sessionId":"1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"deep-singing-taco"}
{"parentUuid":"ad572cd1-988c-4fd6-9d96-3c98ed19cf2a","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"compact_file_reference","filename":"/private/tmp/claude-501/REDACTED/1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb/scratchpad/nexo-work/webapp.py","displayPath":"../../../../../../../../../private/tmp/claude-501/REDACTED/1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb/scratchpad/nexo-work/webapp.py"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d93e61bb-9a1f-4e1a-8f5f-54e3c6f71876","timestamp":"2026-11-02T15:12:26.124Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /private/tmp/claude-501/REDACTED/1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb/scratchpad/nexo-work/webapp.py was read before the last conversation was summarized, but the contents are too large to include. Use Read tool if you need to access it.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/Sagenkazaran/Library/Application Support/Claude/scratch-workspaces/f907b165-4712-485f-a44b-7f7d54b74cf9/77d6453f-aaee-4ad3-a7ea-34b17cbaf2e5/scratch-2026-10-26-b13584","sessionId":"1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"deep-singing-taco"}
{"parentUuid":"d93e61bb-9a1f-4e1a-8f5f-54e3c6f71876","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/private/tmp/claude-501/REDACTED/1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb/scratchpad/nexo-work/tests/test_webapp.py","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-Sagenkazaran-Library-Application-Support-Claude-scratch-workspaces-f907b165-4712-485f-a44b-7f7d54b74cf9-77d6453f-aaee-4ad3-a7ea-34b17cbaf2e5-scratch-2026-10-26-b13584/1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb/scratchpad/nexo-work/tests/test_webapp.py","content":"\"\"\"Web cabinet without Telegram: real routes, SQLite and device provisioning; panels and Platega are fakes.\"\"\"\nimport importlib\nimport os\nimport tempfile\nimport unittest\nfrom unittest.mock import AsyncMock, patch\n\nfrom aiohttp.test_utils import TestClient, TestServer\n\nimport database as db\nimport payments\nimport webapp\nfrom test_devices import Panel\nfrom vpn_service import Node\n\nIPHONE = \"Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 18_0 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 Version/18.0 Mobile/15E148 Safari/604.1\"\nANDROID = \"Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 15; Pixel 9) AppleWebKit/537.36 Chrome/130.0 Mobile Safari/537.36\"\n\n\nclass WebCabinetTests(unittest.IsolatedAsyncioTestCase):\n    async def asyncSetUp(self):\n        self.tmp = tempfile.TemporaryDirectory()\n        self.db_patch = patch.object(db, \"DB_PATH\", self.tmp.name + \"/test.db\")\n        self.db_patch.start()\n        db.init_db()\n        webapp._starts.clear()\n        self.nodes = [Node(k, k, k + \".example\", 443, \"pk\", \"sid\", \"sni\") for k in (\"a\", \"b\")]\n        self.panels = {n.key: Panel() for n in self.nodes}\n        import subscription\n        self.subscription = importlib.reload(subscription)\n        app = self.subscription.create_app(database_module=db, node_provider=lambda: self.nodes,\n                                           public_base_url=\"https://vpn.example\", device_client_factory=self.panels.__getitem__)\n        self.client = TestClient(TestServer(app))\n        await self.client.start_server()\n\n    async def asyncTearDown(self):\n        await self.client.close()\n        self.db_patch.stop()\n        self.tmp.cleanup()\n\n    async def start(self, ua=IPHONE):\n        response = await self.client.post(\"/app/start\", headers={\"User-Agent\": ua}, allow_redirects=False)\n        self.assertEqual(response.status, 303)\n        return response.headers[\"Location\"]\n\n    def web_users(self):\n        return [u for u in db.get_all_users() if u[\"tg_id\"] < 0]\n\n    async def test_landing_offers_trial_and_names_the_device(self):\n        response = await self.client.get(\"/app\", headers={\"User-Agent\": IPHONE})\n        text = await response.text()\n        self.assertEqual(response.status, 200)\n        self.assertIn(\"7 дней бесплатно\", text)\n        self.assertIn(\"Начать на iPhone\", text)\n        self.assertNotIn(\"обход\", text.lower())\n\n    async def test_start_creates_web_account_with_trial_and_iphone_key(self):\n        location = await self.start()\n        self.assertTrue(location.startswith(\"/c/\"))\n        user = self.web_users()[0]\n        self.assertIsNotNone(payments.active_until(user))\n        devices = db.list_devices(user[\"tg_id\"])\n        self.assertEqual([(d[\"platform\"], d[\"status\"]) for d in devices], [(\"ios\", \"active\")])\n        self.assertEqual(len(self.panels[\"a\"].adds), 1)\n\n    async def test_cabinet_shows_karing_steps_for_russian_app_store(self):\n        location = await self.start()\n        response = await self.client.get(location, headers={\"User-Agent\": IPHONE})\n        text = await response.text()\n        self.assertIn(\"Доступ до\", text)\n        self.assertIn(\"id6472431552\", text)\n        self.assertIn(\"karing://install-config?\", text)\n        self.assertIn(\"страну «Россия»\", text)\n        self.assertIn(\"Запасной вариант — OneXray\", text)\n        self.assertIn(\"Скопировать ссылку\", text)\n        self.assertIn(\"nexo_cabinet=\", response.headers[\"Set-Cookie\"])\n        self.assertIn(\"HttpOnly\", response.headers[\"Set-Cookie\"])\n\n    async def test_foreign_app_store_switches_to_happ(self):\n        location = (await self.start()).split(\"?\")[0]\n        text = await (await self.client.get(location + \"?p=ios&store=other\", headers={\"User-Agent\": IPHONE})).text()\n        self.assertIn(\"id6504287215\", text)\n        self.assertIn(\"/happ/install/\", text)\n\n    async def test_another_device_gets_its_own_key_on_request(self):\n        location = (await self.start()).split(\"?\")[0]\n        text = await (await self.client.get(location + \"?p=android\", headers={\"User-Agent\": IPHONE})).text()\n        self.assertIn(\"Создать ключ для Android\", text)\n        response = await self.client.post(location + \"/device?p=android\", allow_redirects=False)\n        self.assertEqual(response.status, 303)\n        user = self.web_users()[0]\n        self.assertEqual(sorted(d[\"platform\"] for d in db.list_devices(user[\"tg_id\"])), [\"android\", \"ios\"])\n        text = await (await self.client.get(location + \"?p=android\", headers={\"User-Agent\": ANDROID})).text()\n        self.assertIn(\"com.happproxy\", text)\n\n    async def test_cookie_reopens_the_cabinet(self):\n        location = (await self.start()).split(\"?\")[0]\n        cookie = (await self.client.get(location, headers={\"User-Agent\": IPHONE})).headers[\"Set-Cookie\"].split(\";\")[0]\n        # the cookie is Secure, so the plain-HTTP test client would not send it back by itself\n        response = await self.client.get(\"/app\", headers={\"Cookie\": cookie}, allow_redirects=False)\n        self.assertEqual(response.status, 302)\n        self.assertEqual(response.headers[\"Location\"], location)\n\n    async def test_unknown_cabinet_is_not_found(self):\n        response = await self.client.get(\"/c/\" + \"x\" * 43)\n        self.assertEqual(response.status, 404)\n\n    async def test_starts_are_limited_per_address(self):\n        for _ in range(webapp.STARTS_PER_IP):\n            await self.start()\n        response = await self.client.post(\"/app/start\", headers={\"User-Agent\": IPHONE}, allow_redirects=False)\n        self.assertEqual(response.status, 429)\n        self.assertEqual(len(self.web_users()), webapp.STARTS_PER_IP)\n\n    async def test_payment_goes_to_platega_and_is_checked_on_return(self):\n        location = (await self.start()).split(\"?\")[0]\n        user = self.web_users()[0]\n        before = payments.active_until(user)\n        request = AsyncMock(return_value={\"transactionId\": \"tx-web\", \"status\": \"PENDING\",\n                                          \"url\": \"https://pay.platega.io/?id=w\", \"expiresIn\": \"00:15:00\"})\n        with patch.multiple(payments, MERCHANT_ID=\"m\", SECRET=\"s\"), patch.object(payments, \"_request\", request):\n            response = await self.client.post(location + \"/pay?tariff=m1\", allow_redirects=False)\n            self.assertEqual(response.headers[\"Location\"], \"https://pay.platega.io/?id=w\")\n            body = request.call_args.args[2]\n            self.assertTrue(body[\"metadata\"][\"user_email\"].endswith(\"@mail.ru\"))\n            self.assertIn(location + \"?check=\", body[\"return\"])\n            request.return_value = {\"status\": \"CONFIRMED\"}\n            text = await (await self.client.get(body[\"return\"].replace(\"https://vpn.example\", \"\"),\n                                                headers={\"User-Agent\": IPHONE})).text()\n        self.assertIn(\"Оплата получена\", text)\n        after = payments.active_until(db.get_user(user[\"tg_id\"]))\n        self.assertEqual((after - before).days, 30)\n\n    async def test_documents_are_public(self):\n        for name in (\"tariffs\", \"terms\", \"privacy\", \"support\"):\n            response = await self.client.get(f\"/docs/{name}\")\n            self.assertEqual(response.status, 200)\n        self.assertIn(\"199\", await (await self.client.get(\"/docs/tariffs\")).text())\n\n    async def test_tokens_are_masked_in_the_request_log(self):\n        location = (await self.start()).split(\"?\")[0]\n        with self.assertLogs(\"AuraVPN.subscription\", level=\"INFO\") as logs:\n            await self.client.get(location)\n        self.assertNotIn(location.split(\"/\")[2], \"\\n\".join(logs.output))\n\n\nclass WebLinkAndExpiryTests(WebCabinetTests):\n    async def test_connect_telegram_opens_the_bot_with_a_one_time_code(self):\n        location = (await self.start()).split(\"?\")[0]\n        text = await (await self.client.get(location, headers={\"User-Agent\": IPHONE})).text()\n        self.assertIn(\"Подключите Telegram\", text)  # step 4, right after «Включите»\n        self.assertLess(text.index(\"Включите\"), text.index(\"Подключите Telegram\"))\n        self.assertEqual(text.count('/telegram\"'), 1)\n        response = await self.client.post(location + \"/telegram\", allow_redirects=False)\n        self.assertEqual(response.status, 303)\n        self.assertRegex(response.headers[\"Location\"], r\"^https://t\\.me/\\w+\\?start=web_[\\w-]+$\")\n\n    async def test_expired_cabinet_asks_to_renew_instead_of_setup(self):\n        location = (await self.start()).split(\"?\")[0]\n        user = self.web_users()[0]\n        conn = db.get_db()\n        conn.execute(\"UPDATE users SET paid_until = '2000-01-01T00:00:00' WHERE tg_id = ?\", (user[\"tg_id\"],))\n        conn.commit()\n        conn.close()\n        text = await (await self.client.get(location, headers={\"User-Agent\": IPHONE})).text()\n        self.assertIn(\"Срок доступа закончился\", text)\n        self.assertIn(\"Не активен\", text)\n        self.assertNotIn(\"Добавить ключ в Karing\", text)\n\n\nclass UnlimitedAccountTests(WebCabinetTests):\n    async def test_account_without_end_date_is_active_with_steps(self):\n        location = (await self.start()).split(\"?\")[0]\n        user = self.web_users()[0]\n        conn = db.get_db()\n        conn.execute(\"UPDATE users SET paid_until = NULL WHERE tg_id = ?\", (user[\"tg_id\"],))\n        conn.commit()\n        conn.close()\n        text = await (await self.client.get(location, headers={\"User-Agent\": IPHONE})).text()\n        self.assertIn(\"Без срока\", text)\n        self.assertNotIn(\"Не активен\", text)\n        self.assertNotIn(\"Срок доступа закончился\", text)\n        self.assertIn(\"Добавить ключ в Karing\", text)\n","numLines":184,"startLine":1,"totalLines":184}},"displayPath":"../../../../../../../../../private/tmp/claude-501/REDACTED/1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb/scratchpad/nexo-work/tests/test_webapp.py"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a7aae6f2-f0a5-4b87-8533-e83a7907d659","timestamp":"2026-11-02T15:12:26.124Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/private/tmp/claude-501/REDACTED/1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb/scratchpad/nexo-work/tests/test_webapp.py\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t\"\"\"Web cabinet without Telegram: real routes, SQLite and device provisioning; panels and Platega are fakes.\"\"\"\n2\timport importlib\n3\timport os\n4\timport tempfile\n5\timport unittest\n6\tfrom unittest.mock import AsyncMock, patch\n7\t\n8\tfrom aiohttp.test_utils import TestClient, TestServer\n9\t\n10\timport database as db\n11\timport payments\n12\timport webapp\n13\tfrom test_devices import Panel\n14\tfrom vpn_service import Node\n15\t\n16\tIPHONE = \"Mozilla/5.0 (iPhone; CPU iPhone OS 18_0 like Mac OS X) AppleWebKit/605.1.15 Version/18.0 Mobile/15E148 Safari/604.1\"\n17\tANDROID = \"Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 15; Pixel 9) AppleWebKit/537.36 Chrome/130.0 Mobile Safari/537.36\"\n18\t\n19\t\n20\tclass WebCabinetTests(unittest.IsolatedAsyncioTestCase):\n21\t    async def asyncSetUp(self):\n22\t        self.tmp = tempfile.TemporaryDirectory()\n23\t        self.db_patch = patch.object(db, \"DB_PATH\", self.tmp.name + \"/test.db\")\n24\t        self.db_patch.start()\n25\t        db.init_db()\n26\t        webapp._starts.clear()\n27\t        self.nodes = [Node(k, k, k + \".example\", 443, \"pk\", \"sid\", \"sni\") for k in (\"a\", \"b\")]\n28\t        self.panels = {n.key: Panel() for n in self.nodes}\n29\t        import subscription\n30\t        self.subscription = importlib.reload(subscription)\n31\t        app = self.subscription.create_app(database_module=db, node_provider=lambda: self.nodes,\n32\t                                           public_base_url=\"https://vpn.example\", device_client_factory=self.panels.__getitem__)\n33\t        self.client = TestClient(TestServer(app))\n34\t        await self.client.start_server()\n35\t\n36\t    async def asyncTearDown(self):\n37\t        await self.client.close()\n38\t        self.db_patch.stop()\n39\t        self.tmp.cleanup()\n40\t\n41\t    async def start(self, ua=IPHONE):\n42\t        response = await self.client.post(\"/app/start\", headers={\"User-Agent\": ua}, allow_redirects=False)\n43\t        self.assertEqual(response.status, 303)\n44\t        return response.headers[\"Location\"]\n45\t\n46\t    def web_users(self):\n47\t        return [u for u in db.get_all_users() if u[\"tg_id\"] < 0]\n48\t\n49\t    async def test_landing_offers_trial_and_names_the_device(self):\n50\t        response = await self.client.get(\"/app\", headers={\"User-Agent\": IPHONE})\n51\t        text = await response.text()\n52\t        self.assertEqual(response.status, 200)\n53\t        self.assertIn(\"7 дней бесплатно\", text)\n54\t        self.assertIn(\"Начать на iPhone\", text)\n55\t        self.assertNotIn(\"обход\", text.lower())\n56\t\n57\t    async def test_start_creates_web_account_with_trial_and_iphone_key(self):\n58\t        location = await self.start()\n59\t        self.assertTrue(location.startswith(\"/c/\"))\n60\t        user = self.web_users()[0]\n61\t        self.assertIsNotNone(payments.active_until(user))\n62\t        devices = db.list_devices(user[\"tg_id\"])\n63\t        self.assertEqual([(d[\"platform\"], d[\"status\"]) for d in devices], [(\"ios\", \"active\")])\n64\t        self.assertEqual(len(self.panels[\"a\"].adds), 1)\n65\t\n66\t    async def test_cabinet_shows_karing_steps_for_russian_app_store(self):\n67\t        location = await self.start()\n68\t        response = await self.client.get(location, headers={\"User-Agent\": IPHONE})\n69\t        text = await response.text()\n70\t        self.assertIn(\"Доступ до\", text)\n71\t        self.assertIn(\"id6472431552\", text)\n72\t        self.assertIn(\"karing://install-config?\", text)\n73\t        self.assertIn(\"страну «Россия»\", text)\n74\t        self.assertIn(\"Запасной вариант — OneXray\", text)\n75\t        self.assertIn(\"Скопировать ссылку\", text)\n76\t        self.assertIn(\"nexo_cabinet=\", response.headers[\"Set-Cookie\"])\n77\t        self.assertIn(\"HttpOnly\", response.headers[\"Set-Cookie\"])\n78\t\n79\t    async def test_foreign_app_store_switches_to_happ(self):\n80\t        location = (await self.start()).split(\"?\")[0]\n81\t        text = await (await self.client.get(location + \"?p=ios&store=other\", headers={\"User-Agent\": IPHONE})).text()\n82\t        self.assertIn(\"id6504287215\", text)\n83\t        self.assertIn(\"/happ/install/\", text)\n84\t\n85\t    async def test_another_device_gets_its_own_key_on_request(self):\n86\t        location = (await self.start()).split(\"?\")[0]\n87\t        text = await (await self.client.get(location + \"?p=android\", headers={\"User-Agent\": IPHONE})).text()\n88\t        self.assertIn(\"Создать ключ для Android\", text)\n89\t        response = await self.client.post(location + \"/device?p=android\", allow_redirects=False)\n90\t        self.assertEqual(response.status, 303)\n91\t        user = self.web_users()[0]\n92\t        self.assertEqual(sorted(d[\"platform\"] for d in db.list_devices(user[\"tg_id\"])), [\"android\", \"ios\"])\n93\t        text = await (await self.client.get(location + \"?p=android\", headers={\"User-Agent\": ANDROID})).text()\n94\t        self.assertIn(\"com.happproxy\", text)\n95\t\n96\t    async def test_cookie_reopens_the_cabinet(self):\n97\t        location = (await self.start()).split(\"?\")[0]\n98\t        cookie = (await self.client.get(location, headers={\"User-Agent\": IPHONE})).headers[\"Set-Cookie\"].split(\";\")[0]\n99\t        # the cookie is Secure, so the plain-HTTP test client would not send it back by itself\n100\t        response = await self.client.get(\"/app\", headers={\"Cookie\": cookie}, allow_redirects=False)\n101\t        self.assertEqual(response.status, 302)\n102\t        self.assertEqual(response.headers[\"Location\"], location)\n103\t\n104\t    async def test_unknown_cabinet_is_not_found(self):\n105\t        response = await self.client.get(\"/c/\" + \"x\" * 43)\n106\t        self.assertEqual(response.status, 404)\n107\t\n108\t    async def test_starts_are_limited_per_address(self):\n109\t        for _ in range(webapp.STARTS_PER_IP):\n110\t            await self.start()\n111\t        response = await self.client.post(\"/app/start\", headers={\"User-Agent\": IPHONE}, allow_redirects=False)\n112\t        self.assertEqual(response.status, 429)\n113\t        self.assertEqual(len(self.web_users()), webapp.STARTS_PER_IP)\n114\t\n115\t    async def test_payment_goes_to_platega_and_is_checked_on_return(self):\n116\t        location = (await self.start()).split(\"?\")[0]\n117\t        user = self.web_users()[0]\n118\t        before = payments.active_until(user)\n119\t        request = AsyncMock(return_value={\"transactionId\": \"tx-web\", \"status\": \"PENDING\",\n120\t                                          \"url\": \"https://pay.platega.io/?id=w\", \"expiresIn\": \"00:15:00\"})\n121\t        with patch.multiple(payments, MERCHANT_ID=\"m\", SECRET=\"s\"), patch.object(payments, \"_request\", request):\n122\t            response = await self.client.post(location + \"/pay?tariff=m1\", allow_redirects=False)\n123\t            self.assertEqual(response.headers[\"Location\"], \"https://pay.platega.io/?id=w\")\n124\t            body = request.call_args.args[2]\n125\t            self.assertTrue(body[\"metadata\"][\"user_email\"].endswith(\"@mail.ru\"))\n126\t            self.assertIn(location + \"?check=\", body[\"return\"])\n127\t            request.return_value = {\"status\": \"CONFIRMED\"}\n128\t            text = await (await self.client.get(body[\"return\"].replace(\"https://vpn.example\", \"\"),\n129\t                                                headers={\"User-Agent\": IPHONE})).text()\n130\t        self.assertIn(\"Оплата получена\", text)\n131\t        after = payments.active_until(db.get_user(user[\"tg_id\"]))\n132\t        self.assertEqual((after - before).days, 30)\n133\t\n134\t    async def test_documents_are_public(self):\n135\t        for name in (\"tariffs\", \"terms\", \"privacy\", \"support\"):\n136\t            response = await self.client.get(f\"/docs/{name}\")\n137\t            self.assertEqual(response.status, 200)\n138\t        self.assertIn(\"199\", await (await self.client.get(\"/docs/tariffs\")).text())\n139\t\n140\t    async def test_tokens_are_masked_in_the_request_log(self):\n141\t        location = (await self.start()).split(\"?\")[0]\n142\t        with self.assertLogs(\"AuraVPN.subscription\", level=\"INFO\") as logs:\n143\t            await self.client.get(location)\n144\t        self.assertNotIn(location.split(\"/\")[2], \"\\n\".join(logs.output))\n145\t\n146\t\n147\tclass WebLinkAndExpiryTests(WebCabinetTests):\n148\t    async def test_connect_telegram_opens_the_bot_with_a_one_time_code(self):\n149\t        location = (await self.start()).split(\"?\")[0]\n150\t        text = await (await self.client.get(location, headers={\"User-Agent\": IPHONE})).text()\n151\t        self.assertIn(\"Подключите Telegram\", text)  # step 4, right after «Включите»\n152\t        self.assertLess(text.index(\"Включите\"), text.index(\"Подключите Telegram\"))\n153\t        self.assertEqual(text.count('/telegram\"'), 1)\n154\t        response = await self.client.post(location + \"/telegram\", allow_redirects=False)\n155\t        self.assertEqual(response.status, 303)\n156\t        self.assertRegex(response.headers[\"Location\"], r\"^https://t\\.me/\\w+\\?start=web_[\\w-]+$\")\n157\t\n158\t    async def test_expired_cabinet_asks_to_renew_instead_of_setup(self):\n159\t        location = (await self.start()).split(\"?\")[0]\n160\t        user = self.web_users()[0]\n161\t        conn = db.get_db()\n162\t        conn.execute(\"UPDATE users SET paid_until = '2000-01-01T00:00:00' WHERE tg_id = ?\", (user[\"tg_id\"],))\n163\t        conn.commit()\n164\t        conn.close()\n165\t        text = await (await self.client.get(location, headers={\"User-Agent\": IPHONE})).text()\n166\t        self.assertIn(\"Срок доступа закончился\", text)\n167\t        self.assertIn(\"Не активен\", text)\n168\t        self.assertNotIn(\"Добавить ключ в Karing\", text)\n169\t\n170\t\n171\tclass UnlimitedAccountTests(WebCabinetTests):\n172\t    async def test_account_without_end_date_is_active_with_steps(self):\n173\t        location = (await self.start()).split(\"?\")[0]\n174\t        user = self.web_users()[0]\n175\t        conn = db.get_db()\n176\t        conn.execute(\"UPDATE users SET paid_until = NULL WHERE tg_id = ?\", (user[\"tg_id\"],))\n177\t        conn.commit()\n178\t        conn.close()\n179\t        text = await (await self.client.get(location, headers={\"User-Agent\": IPHONE})).text()\n180\t        self.assertIn(\"Без срока\", text)\n181\t        self.assertNotIn(\"Не активен\", text)\n182\t        self.assertNotIn(\"Срок доступа закончился\", text)\n183\t        self.assertIn(\"Добавить ключ в Karing\", text)\n184\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/Sagenkazaran/Library/Application Support/Claude/scratch-workspaces/f907b165-4712-485f-a44b-7f7d54b74cf9/77d6453f-aaee-4ad3-a7ea-34b17cbaf2e5/scratch-2026-10-26-b13584","sessionId":"1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"deep-singing-taco"}
{"parentUuid":"a7aae6f2-f0a5-4b87-8533-e83a7907d659","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"invoked_skills","skills":[{"name":"frontend-design","path":"userSettings:frontend-design","content":"Base directory for this skill: /Users/Sagenkazaran/.claude/skills/frontend-design\n\n# Frontend Design\n\nApproach this as the design lead at a small studio known for giving every client a visual identity that could not be mistaken for anyone else's. This client has already rejected proposals that felt templated, and is paying for a distinctive point of view: make deliberate, opinionated choices about palette, typography, and layout that are specific to this brief, and take one real aesthetic risk you can justify.\n\n## Ground it in the subject\n\nIf the brief does not pin down what the product or subject is, pin it yourself before designing: name one concrete subject, its audience, and the page's single job, and state your choice. If there's any information in your memory about the human's preferences, context about what they're building, or designs you've made before – use that as a hint. The subject's own world, its materials, instruments, artifacts, and vernacular, is where distinctive choices come from. Build with the brief's real content and subject matter throughout.\n\n## Design principles\n\nFor web designs, the hero is a thesis. Open with the most characteristic thing in the subject's world, in whatever form makes sense for it: a headline, an image, an animation, a live demo, an interactive moment. Be deliberate with your choice: a big number with a small label, supporting stats, and a gradient accent is the template answer, only use if that's truly the best option.\n\nTypography carries the personality of the page. Pair the display and body faces deliberately, not the same families you would reach for on any other project, and set a clear type scale with intentional weights, widths, and spacing. Make the type treatment itself a memorable part of the design, not a neutral delivery vehicle for the content.\n\nStructure is information. Structural devices, numbering, eyebrows, dividers, labels, should encode something true about the content, not decorate it. Many generic designs use numbered markers (01 / 02 / 03), but that's only appropriate if the content actually is a sequence - like a real process or a typed timeline where order carries information the reader needs. Question if choices like numbered markers actually make sense before incorporating them.\n\nLeverage motion deliberately. Think about where and if animation can serve the subject: a page-load sequence, a scroll-triggered reveal, hover micro-interactions, ambient atmosphere. An orchestrated moment usually lands harder than scattered effects; choose what the direction calls for. However, sometimes less is more, and extra animation contributes to the feeling that the design is AI-generated.\n\nMatch complexity to the vision. Maximalist directions need elaborate execution; minimal directions need precision in spacing, type, and detail. Elegance is executing the chosen vision well.\n\nConsider written content carefully. Often a design brief may not contain real content, and it's up to you to come up with copy. Copy can make a design feel as templated as the design itself. See the below section on writing for more guidance.\n\n## Process: brainstorm, explore, plan, critique, build, critique again\n\nFor calibration: AI-generated design right now clusters around three looks: (1) a warm cream background (near #F4F1EA) with a high-contrast serif display and a terracotta accent; (2) a near-black background with a single bright acid-green or vermilion accent; (3) a broadsheet-style layout with hairline rules, zero border-radius, and dense newspaper-like columns. All three are legitimate for some briefs, but they are defaults rather than choices, and they appear regardless of subject. Where the brief pins down a visual direction, follow it exactly — the brief's own words always win, including when it asks for one of these looks. Where it leaves an axis free, don't spend that freedom on one of these defaults. Just like a human designer who's hired, there's often a careful balance between doing what you're good at and taking each project as a chance to experiment and learn.\n\nWork in two passes. First, brainstorm a short design plan based on the human's design brief: create a compact token system with color, type, layout, and signature. Color: describe the palette as 4–6 named hex values. Type: the typefaces for 2+ roles (a characterful display face that's used with restraint, a complementary body face, and a utility face for captions or data if needed). Layout: a layout concept, using one-sentence prose descriptions and ASCII wireframes to ideate and compare. Signature: the single unique element this page will be remembered by that embodies the brief in an appropriate way.\n\nThen review that plan against the brief before building: if any part of it reads like the generic default you would produce for any similar page (work through a similar prompt to see if you arrive somewhere similar) rather than a choice made for this specific brief — revise that part, say what you changed and why. Only after you've confirmed the relative uniqueness of your design plan should you start to write the code, following the revised plan exactly and deriving every color and type decision from it.\n\nWhen writing the code, be careful of structuring your CSS selector specificities. It's easy to generate CSS classes that cancel each other out (especially with a type-based selector like .section and a element-based selector like .cta). This can happen often with paddings/margins between sections.\n\nTry to do a lot of this planning and iteration in your thinking, and only show ideas to the user when you have higher confidence it'll delight them.\n\n## Restraint and self-critique\n\nSpend your boldness in one place. Let the signature element be the one memorable thing, keep everything around it quiet and disciplined, and cut any decoration that does not serve the brief. Not taking a risk can be a risk itself! Build to a quality floor without announcing it: responsive down to mobile, visible keyboard focus, reduced motion respected. Critique your own work as you build, taking screenshots if your environment supports it – a picture is worth 1000 tokens. Consider Chanel's advice: before leaving the house, take a look in the mirror and remove one accessory. Human creators have memory and always try to do something new, so if you have a space to quickly jot down notes about what you've tried, it can help you in future passes.\n\n## More on writing in design\n\nWords appear in a design for one reason: to make it easier to understand, and therefore easier to use. They are design material, not decoration. Bring the same intentionality to copy that you would bring to spacing and color. Before writing anything, ask what the design needs to say, and how it can best be said to help the person navigate the experience.\n\nWrite from the end user's side of the screen. Name things by what people control and recognize, never by how the system is built. A person manages notifications, not webhook config. Describe what something does in plain terms rather than selling it. Being specific is always better than being clever.\n\nUse active voice as default. A control should say exactly what happens when it's used: \"Save changes,\" not \"Submit.\" An action keeps the same name through the whole flow, so the button that says \"Publish\" produces a toast that says \"Published.\" The vocabulary of an interface is the signposting for someone navigating the product. Cohesion and consistency are how people learn their way around.\n\nTreat failure and emptiness as moments for direction, not mood. Explain what went wrong and how to fix it, in the interface's voice rather than a person's. Errors don't apologize, and they are never vague about what happened. An empty screen is an invitation to act.\n\nKeep the register conversational and tuned: plain verbs, sentence case, no filler, with tone matched to the brand and the audience. Let each element do exactly one job. A label labels, an example demonstrates, and nothing quietly does double duty.\n\n\nARGUMENTS: Redesign the Nexo web cabinet (mobile-first VPN onboarding web app, Russian UI) so it doesn't look AI-generated/templated"},{"name":"design","path":"userSettings:design","content":"Base directory for this skill: /Users/Sagenkazaran/.claude/skills/design\n\n# Design\n\nUnified design skill: brand, tokens, UI, logo, CIP, slides, banners, social photos, icons.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Brand identity, voice, assets\n- Design system tokens and specs\n- UI styling with shadcn/ui + Tailwind\n- Logo design and AI generation\n- Corporate identity program (CIP) deliverables\n- Presentations and pitch decks\n- Banner design for social media, ads, web, print\n- Social photos for Instagram, Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Pinterest, TikTok\n\n## Sub-skill Routing\n\n| Task | Sub-skill | Details |\n|------|-----------|---------|\n| Brand identity, voice, assets | `brand` | External skill |\n| Tokens, specs, CSS vars | `design-system` | External skill |\n| shadcn/ui, Tailwind, code | `ui-styling` | External skill |\n| Logo creation, AI generation | Logo (built-in) | `references/logo-design.md` |\n| CIP mockups, deliverables | CIP (built-in) | `references/cip-design.md` |\n| Presentations, pitch decks | Slides (built-in) | `references/slides.md` |\n| Banners, covers, headers | Banner (built-in) | `references/banner-sizes-and-styles.md` |\n| Social media images/photos | Social Photos (built-in) | `references/social-photos-design.md` |\n| SVG icons, icon sets | Icon (built-in) | `references/icon-design.md` |\n\n## Logo Design (Built-in)\n\n55+ styles, 30 color palettes, 25 industry guides. Gemini Nano Banana models.\n\n### Logo: Generate Design Brief\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/logo/search.py \"tech startup modern\" --design-brief -p \"BrandName\"\n```\n\n### Logo: Search Styles/Colors/Industries\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/logo/search.py \"minimalist clean\" --domain style\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/logo/search.py \"tech professional\" --domain color\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/logo/search.py \"healthcare medical\" --domain industry\n```\n\n### Logo: Generate with AI\n\n**ALWAYS** generate output logo images with white background.\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/logo/generate.py --brand \"TechFlow\" --style minimalist --industry tech\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/logo/generate.py --prompt \"coffee shop vintage badge\" --style vintage\n```\n\n**IMPORTANT:** When scripts fail, try to fix them directly.\n\nAfter generation, **ALWAYS** ask user about HTML preview via `AskUserQuestion`. If yes, invoke `/ui-ux-pro-max` for gallery.\n\n## CIP Design (Built-in)\n\n50+ deliverables, 20 styles, 20 industries. Gemini Nano Banana (Flash/Pro).\n\n### CIP: Generate Brief\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/cip/search.py \"tech startup\" --cip-brief -b \"BrandName\"\n```\n\n### CIP: Search Domains\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/cip/search.py \"business card letterhead\" --domain deliverable\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/cip/search.py \"luxury premium elegant\" --domain style\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/cip/search.py \"hospitality hotel\" --domain industry\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/cip/search.py \"office reception\" --domain mockup\n```\n\n### CIP: Generate Mockups\n\n```bash\n# With logo (RECOMMENDED)\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/cip/generate.py --brand \"TopGroup\" --logo /path/to/logo.png --deliverable \"business card\" --industry \"consulting\"\n\n# Full CIP set\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/cip/generate.py --brand \"TopGroup\" --logo /path/to/logo.png --industry \"consulting\" --set\n\n# Pro model (4K text)\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/cip/generate.py --brand \"TopGroup\" --logo logo.png --deliverable \"business card\" --model pro\n\n# Without logo\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/cip/generate.py --brand \"TechFlow\" --deliverable \"business card\" --no-logo-prompt\n```\n\nModels: `flash` (default, `gemini-2.5-flash-image`), `pro` (`gemini-3-pro-image-preview`)\n\n### CIP: Render HTML Presentation\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/cip/render-html.py --brand \"TopGroup\" --industry \"consulting\" --images /path/to/cip-output\n```\n\n**Tip:** If no logo exists, use Logo Design section above first.\n\n## Slides (Built-in)\n\nStrategic HTML presentations with Chart.js, design tokens, copywriting formulas.\n\nLoad `references/slides-create.md` for the creation workflow.\n\n### Slides: Knowledge Base\n\n| Topic | File |\n|-------|------|\n| Creation Guide | `references/slides-create.md` |\n| Layout Patterns | `references/slides-layout-patterns.md` |\n| HTML Template | `references/slides-html-template.md` |\n| Copywriting | `references/slides-copywriting-formulas.md` |\n| Strategies | `references/slides-strategies.md` |\n\n## Banner Design (Built-in)\n\n22 art direction styles across social, ads, web, print. Uses `frontend-design`, `ai-artist`, `ai-multimodal`, `chrome-devtools` skills.\n\nLoad `references/banner-sizes-and-styles.md` for complete sizes and styles reference.\n\n### Banner: Workflow\n\n1. **Gather requirements** via `AskUserQuestion` — purpose, platform, content, brand, style, quantity\n2. **Research** — Activate `ui-ux-pro-max`, browse Pinterest for references\n3. **Design** — Create HTML/CSS banner with `frontend-design`, generate visuals with `ai-artist`/`ai-multimodal`\n4. **Export** — Screenshot to PNG at exact dimensions via `chrome-devtools`\n5. **Present** — Show all options side-by-side, iterate on feedback\n\n### Banner: Quick Size Reference\n\n| Platform | Type | Size (px) |\n|----------|------|-----------|\n| Facebook | Cover | 820 x 312 |\n| Twitter/X | Header | 1500 x 500 |\n| LinkedIn | Personal | 1584 x 396 |\n| YouTube | Channel art | 2560 x 1440 |\n| Instagram | Story | 1080 x 1920 |\n| Instagram | Post | 1080 x 1080 |\n| Google Ads | Med Rectangle | 300 x 250 |\n| Website | Hero | 1920 x 600-1080 |\n\n### Banner: Top Art Styles\n\n| Style | Best For |\n|-------|----------|\n| Minimalist | SaaS, tech |\n| Bold Typography | Announcements |\n| Gradient | Modern brands |\n| Photo-Based | Lifestyle, e-com |\n| Geometric | Tech, fintech |\n| Glassmorphism | SaaS, apps |\n| Neon/Cyberpunk | Gaming, events |\n\n### Banner: Design Rules\n\n- Safe zones: critical content in central 70-80%\n- One CTA per banner, bottom-right, min 44px height\n- Max 2 fonts, min 16px body, ≥32px headline\n- Text under 20% for ads (Meta penalizes)\n- Print: 300 DPI, CMYK, 3-5mm bleed\n\n## Icon Design (Built-in)\n\n15 styles, 12 categories. Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview generates SVG text output.\n\n### Icon: Generate Single Icon\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/icon/generate.py --prompt \"settings gear\" --style outlined\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/icon/generate.py --prompt \"shopping cart\" --style filled --color \"#6366F1\"\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/icon/generate.py --name \"dashboard\" --category navigation --style duotone\n```\n\n### Icon: Generate Batch Variations\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/icon/generate.py --prompt \"cloud upload\" --batch 4 --output-dir ./icons\n```\n\n### Icon: Multi-size Export\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/icon/generate.py --prompt \"user profile\" --sizes \"16,24,32,48\" --output-dir ./icons\n```\n\n### Icon: Top Styles\n\n| Style | Best For |\n|-------|----------|\n| outlined | UI interfaces, web apps |\n| filled | Mobile apps, nav bars |\n| duotone | Marketing, landing pages |\n| rounded | Friendly apps, health |\n| sharp | Tech, fintech, enterprise |\n| flat | Material design, Google-style |\n| gradient | Modern brands, SaaS |\n\n**Model:** `gemini-3.1-pro-preview` — text-only output (SVG is XML text). No image generation API needed.\n\n## Social Photos (Built-in)\n\nMulti-platform social image design: HTML/CSS → screenshot export. Uses `ui-ux-pro-max`, `brand`, `design-system`, `chrome-devtools` skills.\n\nLoad `references/social-photos-design.md` for sizes, templates, best practices.\n\n### Social Photos: Workflow\n\n1. **Orchestrate** — `project-management` skill for TODO tasks; parallel subagents for independent work\n2. **Analyze** — Parse prompt: subject, platforms, style, brand context, content elements\n3. **Ideate** — 3-5 concepts, present via `AskUserQuestion`\n4. **Design** — `/ckm:brand` → `/ckm:design-system` → randomly invoke `/ck:ui-ux-pro-max` OR `/ck:frontend-design`; HTML per idea × size\n5. **Export** — `chrome-devtools` or Playwright screenshot at exact px (2x deviceScaleFactor)\n6. **Verify** — Use Chrome MCP or `chrome-devtools` skill to visually inspect exported designs; fix layout/styling issues and re-export\n7. **Report** — Summary to `plans/reports/` with design decisions\n8. **Organize** — Invoke `assets-organizing` skill to sort output files and reports\n\n### Social Photos: Key Sizes\n\n| Platform | Size (px) | Platform | Size (px) |\n|----------|-----------|----------|-----------|\n| IG Post | 1080×1080 | FB Post | 1200×630 |\n| IG Story | 1080×1920 | X Post | 1200×675 |\n| IG Carousel | 1080×1350 | LinkedIn | 1200×627 |\n| YT Thumb | 1280×720 | Pinterest | 1000×1500 |\n\n## Workflows\n\n### Complete Brand Package\n\n1. **Logo** → `scripts/logo/generate.py` → Generate logo variants\n2. **CIP** → `scripts/cip/generate.py --logo ...` → Create deliverable mockups\n3. **Presentation** → Load `references/slides-create.md` → Build pitch deck\n\n### New Design System\n\n1. **Brand** (brand skill) → Define colors, typography, voice\n2. **Tokens** (design-system skill) → Create semantic token layers\n3. **Implement** (ui-styling skill) → Configure Tailwind, shadcn/ui\n\n## References\n\n| Topic | File |\n|-------|------|\n| Design Routing | `references/design-routing.md` |\n| Logo Design Guide | `references/logo-design.md` |\n| Logo Styles | `references/logo-style-guide.md` |\n| Logo Colors | `references/logo-color-psychology.md` |\n| Logo Prompts | `references/logo-prompt-engineering.md` |\n| CIP Design Guide | `references/cip-design.md` |\n| CIP Deliverables | `references/cip-deliverable-guide.md` |\n| CIP Styles | `references/cip-style-guide.md` |\n| CIP Prompts | `references/cip-prompt-engineering.md` |\n| Slides Create | `references/slides-create.md` |\n| Slides Layouts | `references/slides-layout-patterns.md` |\n| Slides Template | `references/slides-html-template.md` |\n| Slides Copy | `references/slides-copywriting-formulas.md` |\n| Slides Strategy | `references/slides-strategies.md` |\n| Banner Sizes & Styles | `references/banner-sizes-and-styles.md` |\n| Social Photos Guide | `references/social-photos-design.md` |\n| Icon Design Guide | `references/icon-design.md` |\n\n## Scripts\n\n| Script | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| `scripts/logo/search.py` | Search logo styles, colors, industries |\n| `scripts/logo/generate.py` | Generate logos with Gemini AI |\n| `scripts/logo/core.py` | BM25 search engine for logo data |\n| `scripts/cip/search.py` | Search CIP deliverables, styles, industries |\n| `scripts/cip/generate.py` | Generate CIP mockups with Gemini |\n| `scripts/cip/render-html.py` | Render HTML presentation from CIP mockups |\n| `scripts/cip/core.py` | BM25 search engine for CIP data |\n| `scripts/icon/generate.py` | Generate SVG icons with Gemini 3.1 Pro |\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n**Python:** This skill uses Python scripts. On Windows, use `python` instead of `python3` (e.g., `python scripts/logo/search.py` instead of `python3 scripts/logo/search.py`).\n\nCheck if Python is installed:\n```bash\npython3 --version || python --version\n```\n\n## Setup\n\n```bash\nexport GEMINI_API_KEY=\"your-key\"  # https://aistudio.google.com/apikey\npip install google-genai pillow\n```\n\n> **Note for Windows:** Use `python` instead of `pip` where needed (e.g., `python -m pip install ...`).\n\n## Integration\n\n**External sub-skills:** brand, design-system, ui-styling\n**Related Skills:** frontend-design, ui-ux-pro-max, ai-multimodal, chrome-devtools\n\n\nARGUMENTS: design logo for \"Nexo\" — VPN / secure connection service; strict, corporate, minimal; symbol of connection/link; generate via Gemini (user asked for the Gemini 2.5 logo generator)"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3d84db02-372c-48b1-a1df-c23d7e5ea8b1","timestamp":"2026-11-02T15:12:26.129Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nThe following skills were invoked EARLIER in this session (before the conversation was compacted), not on the current turn. They are shown here for context only so you remain aware of their guidelines.\n\nIMPORTANT: Do NOT re-execute these skills or perform their one-time setup actions (e.g., scheduling, creating files) again. Any request or argument text embedded in the skill bodies below — for example under a \"## User Request\" or \"## Input\" heading — was captured when that skill was first invoked. It is NOT the user's current message and NOT a new request: do not act on it as if it were live. Only continue to apply ongoing behavioral guidelines from these skills where still relevant.\n\n### Skill: frontend-design\nPath: userSettings:frontend-design\n\nBase directory for this skill: /Users/Sagenkazaran/.claude/skills/frontend-design\n\n# Frontend Design\n\nApproach this as the design lead at a small studio known for giving every client a visual identity that could not be mistaken for anyone else's. This client has already rejected proposals that felt templated, and is paying for a distinctive point of view: make deliberate, opinionated choices about palette, typography, and layout that are specific to this brief, and take one real aesthetic risk you can justify.\n\n## Ground it in the subject\n\nIf the brief does not pin down what the product or subject is, pin it yourself before designing: name one concrete subject, its audience, and the page's single job, and state your choice. If there's any information in your memory about the human's preferences, context about what they're building, or designs you've made before – use that as a hint. The subject's own world, its materials, instruments, artifacts, and vernacular, is where distinctive choices come from. Build with the brief's real content and subject matter throughout.\n\n## Design principles\n\nFor web designs, the hero is a thesis. Open with the most characteristic thing in the subject's world, in whatever form makes sense for it: a headline, an image, an animation, a live demo, an interactive moment. Be deliberate with your choice: a big number with a small label, supporting stats, and a gradient accent is the template answer, only use if that's truly the best option.\n\nTypography carries the personality of the page. Pair the display and body faces deliberately, not the same families you would reach for on any other project, and set a clear type scale with intentional weights, widths, and spacing. Make the type treatment itself a memorable part of the design, not a neutral delivery vehicle for the content.\n\nStructure is information. Structural devices, numbering, eyebrows, dividers, labels, should encode something true about the content, not decorate it. Many generic designs use numbered markers (01 / 02 / 03), but that's only appropriate if the content actually is a sequence - like a real process or a typed timeline where order carries information the reader needs. Question if choices like numbered markers actually make sense before incorporating them.\n\nLeverage motion deliberately. Think about where and if animation can serve the subject: a page-load sequence, a scroll-triggered reveal, hover micro-interactions, ambient atmosphere. An orchestrated moment usually lands harder than scattered effects; choose what the direction calls for. However, sometimes less is more, and extra animation contributes to the feeling that the design is AI-generated.\n\nMatch complexity to the vision. Maximalist directions need elaborate execution; minimal directions need precision in spacing, type, and detail. Elegance is executing the chosen vision well.\n\nConsider written content carefully. Often a design brief may not contain real content, and it's up to you to come up with copy. Copy can make a design feel as templated as the design itself. See the below section on writing for more guidance.\n\n## Process: brainstorm, explore, plan, critique, build, critique again\n\nFor calibration: AI-generated design right now clusters around three looks: (1) a warm cream background (near #F4F1EA) with a high-contrast serif display and a terracotta accent; (2) a near-black background with a single bright acid-green or vermilion accent; (3) a broadsheet-style layout with hairline rules, zero border-radius, and dense newspaper-like columns. All three are legitimate for some briefs, but they are defaults rather than choices, and they appear regardless of subject. Where the brief pins down a visual direction, follow it exactly — the brief's own words always win, including when it asks for one of these looks. Where it leaves an axis free, don't spend that freedom on one of these defaults. Just like a human designer who's hired, there's often a careful balance between doing what you're good at and taking each project as a chance to experiment and learn.\n\nWork in two passes. First, brainstorm a short design plan based on the human's design brief: create a compact token system with color, type, layout, and signature. Color: describe the palette as 4–6 named hex values. Type: the typefaces for 2+ roles (a characterful display face that's used with restraint, a complementary body face, and a utility face for captions or data if needed). Layout: a layout concept, using one-sentence prose descriptions and ASCII wireframes to ideate and compare. Signature: the single unique element this page will be remembered by that embodies the brief in an appropriate way.\n\nThen review that plan against the brief before building: if any part of it reads like the generic default you would produce for any similar page (work through a similar prompt to see if you arrive somewhere similar) rather than a choice made for this specific brief — revise that part, say what you changed and why. Only after you've confirmed the relative uniqueness of your design plan should you start to write the code, following the revised plan exactly and deriving every color and type decision from it.\n\nWhen writing the code, be careful of structuring your CSS selector specificities. It's easy to generate CSS classes that cancel each other out (especially with a type-based selector like .section and a element-based selector like .cta). This can happen often with paddings/margins between sections.\n\nTry to do a lot of this planning and iteration in your thinking, and only show ideas to the user when you have higher confidence it'll delight them.\n\n## Restraint and self-critique\n\nSpend your boldness in one place. Let the signature element be the one memorable thing, keep everything around it quiet and disciplined, and cut any decoration that does not serve the brief. Not taking a risk can be a risk itself! Build to a quality floor without announcing it: responsive down to mobile, visible keyboard focus, reduced motion respected. Critique your own work as you build, taking screenshots if your environment supports it – a picture is worth 1000 tokens. Consider Chanel's advice: before leaving the house, take a look in the mirror and remove one accessory. Human creators have memory and always try to do something new, so if you have a space to quickly jot down notes about what you've tried, it can help you in future passes.\n\n## More on writing in design\n\nWords appear in a design for one reason: to make it easier to understand, and therefore easier to use. They are design material, not decoration. Bring the same intentionality to copy that you would bring to spacing and color. Before writing anything, ask what the design needs to say, and how it can best be said to help the person navigate the experience.\n\nWrite from the end user's side of the screen. Name things by what people control and recognize, never by how the system is built. A person manages notifications, not webhook config. Describe what something does in plain terms rather than selling it. Being specific is always better than being clever.\n\nUse active voice as default. A control should say exactly what happens when it's used: \"Save changes,\" not \"Submit.\" An action keeps the same name through the whole flow, so the button that says \"Publish\" produces a toast that says \"Published.\" The vocabulary of an interface is the signposting for someone navigating the product. Cohesion and consistency are how people learn their way around.\n\nTreat failure and emptiness as moments for direction, not mood. Explain what went wrong and how to fix it, in the interface's voice rather than a person's. Errors don't apologize, and they are never vague about what happened. An empty screen is an invitation to act.\n\nKeep the register conversational and tuned: plain verbs, sentence case, no filler, with tone matched to the brand and the audience. Let each element do exactly one job. A label labels, an example demonstrates, and nothing quietly does double duty.\n\n\nARGUMENTS: Redesign the Nexo web cabinet (mobile-first VPN onboarding web app, Russian UI) so it doesn't look AI-generated/templated\n\n---\n\n### Skill: design\nPath: userSettings:design\n\nBase directory for this skill: /Users/Sagenkazaran/.claude/skills/design\n\n# Design\n\nUnified design skill: brand, tokens, UI, logo, CIP, slides, banners, social photos, icons.\n\n## When to Use\n\n- Brand identity, voice, assets\n- Design system tokens and specs\n- UI styling with shadcn/ui + Tailwind\n- Logo design and AI generation\n- Corporate identity program (CIP) deliverables\n- Presentations and pitch decks\n- Banner design for social media, ads, web, print\n- Social photos for Instagram, Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, Pinterest, TikTok\n\n## Sub-skill Routing\n\n| Task | Sub-skill | Details |\n|------|-----------|---------|\n| Brand identity, voice, assets | `brand` | External skill |\n| Tokens, specs, CSS vars | `design-system` | External skill |\n| shadcn/ui, Tailwind, code | `ui-styling` | External skill |\n| Logo creation, AI generation | Logo (built-in) | `references/logo-design.md` |\n| CIP mockups, deliverables | CIP (built-in) | `references/cip-design.md` |\n| Presentations, pitch decks | Slides (built-in) | `references/slides.md` |\n| Banners, covers, headers | Banner (built-in) | `references/banner-sizes-and-styles.md` |\n| Social media images/photos | Social Photos (built-in) | `references/social-photos-design.md` |\n| SVG icons, icon sets | Icon (built-in) | `references/icon-design.md` |\n\n## Logo Design (Built-in)\n\n55+ styles, 30 color palettes, 25 industry guides. Gemini Nano Banana models.\n\n### Logo: Generate Design Brief\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/logo/search.py \"tech startup modern\" --design-brief -p \"BrandName\"\n```\n\n### Logo: Search Styles/Colors/Industries\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/logo/search.py \"minimalist clean\" --domain style\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/logo/search.py \"tech professional\" --domain color\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/logo/search.py \"healthcare medical\" --domain industry\n```\n\n### Logo: Generate with AI\n\n**ALWAYS** generate output logo images with white background.\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/logo/generate.py --brand \"TechFlow\" --style minimalist --industry tech\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/logo/generate.py --prompt \"coffee shop vintage badge\" --style vintage\n```\n\n**IMPORTANT:** When scripts fail, try to fix them directly.\n\nAfter generation, **ALWAYS** ask user about HTML preview via `AskUserQuestion`. If yes, invoke `/ui-ux-pro-max` for gallery.\n\n## CIP Design (Built-in)\n\n50+ deliverables, 20 styles, 20 industries. Gemini Nano Banana (Flash/Pro).\n\n### CIP: Generate Brief\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/cip/search.py \"tech startup\" --cip-brief -b \"BrandName\"\n```\n\n### CIP: Search Domains\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/cip/search.py \"business card letterhead\" --domain deliverable\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/cip/search.py \"luxury premium elegant\" --domain style\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/cip/search.py \"hospitality hotel\" --domain industry\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/cip/search.py \"office reception\" --domain mockup\n```\n\n### CIP: Generate Mockups\n\n```bash\n# With logo (RECOMMENDED)\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/cip/generate.py --brand \"TopGroup\" --logo /path/to/logo.png --deliverable \"business card\" --industry \"consulting\"\n\n# Full CIP set\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/cip/generate.py --brand \"TopGroup\" --logo /path/to/logo.png --industry \"consulting\" --set\n\n# Pro model (4K text)\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/cip/generate.py --brand \"TopGroup\" --logo logo.png --deliverable \"business card\" --model pro\n\n# Without logo\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/cip/generate.py --brand \"TechFlow\" --deliverable \"business card\" --no-logo-prompt\n```\n\nModels: `flash` (default, `gemini-2.5-flash-image`), `pro` (`gemini-3-pro-image-preview`)\n\n### CIP: Render HTML Presentation\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/cip/render-html.py --brand \"TopGroup\" --industry \"consulting\" --images /path/to/cip-output\n```\n\n**Tip:** If no logo exists, use Logo Design section above first.\n\n## Slides (Built-in)\n\nStrategic HTML presentations with Chart.js, design tokens, copywriting formulas.\n\nLoad `references/slides-create.md` for the creation workflow.\n\n### Slides: Knowledge Base\n\n| Topic | File |\n|-------|------|\n| Creation Guide | `references/slides-create.md` |\n| Layout Patterns | `references/slides-layout-patterns.md` |\n| HTML Template | `references/slides-html-template.md` |\n| Copywriting | `references/slides-copywriting-formulas.md` |\n| Strategies | `references/slides-strategies.md` |\n\n## Banner Design (Built-in)\n\n22 art direction styles across social, ads, web, print. Uses `frontend-design`, `ai-artist`, `ai-multimodal`, `chrome-devtools` skills.\n\nLoad `references/banner-sizes-and-styles.md` for complete sizes and styles reference.\n\n### Banner: Workflow\n\n1. **Gather requirements** via `AskUserQuestion` — purpose, platform, content, brand, style, quantity\n2. **Research** — Activate `ui-ux-pro-max`, browse Pinterest for references\n3. **Design** — Create HTML/CSS banner with `frontend-design`, generate visuals with `ai-artist`/`ai-multimodal`\n4. **Export** — Screenshot to PNG at exact dimensions via `chrome-devtools`\n5. **Present** — Show all options side-by-side, iterate on feedback\n\n### Banner: Quick Size Reference\n\n| Platform | Type | Size (px) |\n|----------|------|-----------|\n| Facebook | Cover | 820 x 312 |\n| Twitter/X | Header | 1500 x 500 |\n| LinkedIn | Personal | 1584 x 396 |\n| YouTube | Channel art | 2560 x 1440 |\n| Instagram | Story | 1080 x 1920 |\n| Instagram | Post | 1080 x 1080 |\n| Google Ads | Med Rectangle | 300 x 250 |\n| Website | Hero | 1920 x 600-1080 |\n\n### Banner: Top Art Styles\n\n| Style | Best For |\n|-------|----------|\n| Minimalist | SaaS, tech |\n| Bold Typography | Announcements |\n| Gradient | Modern brands |\n| Photo-Based | Lifestyle, e-com |\n| Geometric | Tech, fintech |\n| Glassmorphism | SaaS, apps |\n| Neon/Cyberpunk | Gaming, events |\n\n### Banner: Design Rules\n\n- Safe zones: critical content in central 70-80%\n- One CTA per banner, bottom-right, min 44px height\n- Max 2 fonts, min 16px body, ≥32px headline\n- Text under 20% for ads (Meta penalizes)\n- Print: 300 DPI, CMYK, 3-5mm bleed\n\n## Icon Design (Built-in)\n\n15 styles, 12 categories. Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview generates SVG text output.\n\n### Icon: Generate Single Icon\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/icon/generate.py --prompt \"settings gear\" --style outlined\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/icon/generate.py --prompt \"shopping cart\" --style filled --color \"#6366F1\"\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/icon/generate.py --name \"dashboard\" --category navigation --style duotone\n```\n\n### Icon: Generate Batch Variations\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/icon/generate.py --prompt \"cloud upload\" --batch 4 --output-dir ./icons\n```\n\n### Icon: Multi-size Export\n\n```bash\npython3 ~/.claude/skills/design/scripts/icon/generate.py --prompt \"user profile\" --sizes \"16,24,32,48\" --output-dir ./icons\n```\n\n### Icon: Top Styles\n\n| Style | Best For |\n|-------|----------|\n| outlined | UI interfaces, web apps |\n| filled | Mobile apps, nav bars |\n| duotone | Marketing, landing pages |\n| rounded | Friendly apps, health |\n| sharp | Tech, fintech, enterprise |\n| flat | Material design, Google-style |\n| gradient | Modern brands, SaaS |\n\n**Model:** `gemini-3.1-pro-preview` — text-only output (SVG is XML text). No image generation API needed.\n\n## Social Photos (Built-in)\n\nMulti-platform social image design: HTML/CSS → screenshot export. Uses `ui-ux-pro-max`, `brand`, `design-system`, `chrome-devtools` skills.\n\nLoad `references/social-photos-design.md` for sizes, templates, best practices.\n\n### Social Photos: Workflow\n\n1. **Orchestrate** — `project-management` skill for TODO tasks; parallel subagents for independent work\n2. **Analyze** — Parse prompt: subject, platforms, style, brand context, content elements\n3. **Ideate** — 3-5 concepts, present via `AskUserQuestion`\n4. **Design** — `/ckm:brand` → `/ckm:design-system` → randomly invoke `/ck:ui-ux-pro-max` OR `/ck:frontend-design`; HTML per idea × size\n5. **Export** — `chrome-devtools` or Playwright screenshot at exact px (2x deviceScaleFactor)\n6. **Verify** — Use Chrome MCP or `chrome-devtools` skill to visually inspect exported designs; fix layout/styling issues and re-export\n7. **Report** — Summary to `plans/reports/` with design decisions\n8. **Organize** — Invoke `assets-organizing` skill to sort output files and reports\n\n### Social Photos: Key Sizes\n\n| Platform | Size (px) | Platform | Size (px) |\n|----------|-----------|----------|-----------|\n| IG Post | 1080×1080 | FB Post | 1200×630 |\n| IG Story | 1080×1920 | X Post | 1200×675 |\n| IG Carousel | 1080×1350 | LinkedIn | 1200×627 |\n| YT Thumb | 1280×720 | Pinterest | 1000×1500 |\n\n## Workflows\n\n### Complete Brand Package\n\n1. **Logo** → `scripts/logo/generate.py` → Generate logo variants\n2. **CIP** → `scripts/cip/generate.py --logo ...` → Create deliverable mockups\n3. **Presentation** → Load `references/slides-create.md` → Build pitch deck\n\n### New Design System\n\n1. **Brand** (brand skill) → Define colors, typography, voice\n2. **Tokens** (design-system skill) → Create semantic token layers\n3. **Implement** (ui-styling skill) → Configure Tailwind, shadcn/ui\n\n## References\n\n| Topic | File |\n|-------|------|\n| Design Routing | `references/design-routing.md` |\n| Logo Design Guide | `references/logo-design.md` |\n| Logo Styles | `references/logo-style-guide.md` |\n| Logo Colors | `references/logo-color-psychology.md` |\n| Logo Prompts | `references/logo-prompt-engineering.md` |\n| CIP Design Guide | `references/cip-design.md` |\n| CIP Deliverables | `references/cip-deliverable-guide.md` |\n| CIP Styles | `references/cip-style-guide.md` |\n| CIP Prompts | `references/cip-prompt-engineering.md` |\n| Slides Create | `references/slides-create.md` |\n| Slides Layouts | `references/slides-layout-patterns.md` |\n| Slides Template | `references/slides-html-template.md` |\n| Slides Copy | `references/slides-copywriting-formulas.md` |\n| Slides Strategy | `references/slides-strategies.md` |\n| Banner Sizes & Styles | `references/banner-sizes-and-styles.md` |\n| Social Photos Guide | `references/social-photos-design.md` |\n| Icon Design Guide | `references/icon-design.md` |\n\n## Scripts\n\n| Script | Purpose |\n|--------|---------|\n| `scripts/logo/search.py` | Search logo styles, colors, industries |\n| `scripts/logo/generate.py` | Generate logos with Gemini AI |\n| `scripts/logo/core.py` | BM25 search engine for logo data |\n| `scripts/cip/search.py` | Search CIP deliverables, styles, industries |\n| `scripts/cip/generate.py` | Generate CIP mockups with Gemini |\n| `scripts/cip/render-html.py` | Render HTML presentation from CIP mockups |\n| `scripts/cip/core.py` | BM25 search engine for CIP data |\n| `scripts/icon/generate.py` | Generate SVG icons with Gemini 3.1 Pro |\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n**Python:** This skill uses Python scripts. On Windows, use `python` instead of `python3` (e.g., `python scripts/logo/search.py` instead of `python3 scripts/logo/search.py`).\n\nCheck if Python is installed:\n```bash\npython3 --version || python --version\n```\n\n## Setup\n\n```bash\nexport GEMINI_API_KEY=\"your-key\"  # https://aistudio.google.com/apikey\npip install google-genai pillow\n```\n\n> **Note for Windows:** Use `python` instead of `pip` where needed (e.g., `python -m pip install ...`).\n\n## Integration\n\n**External sub-skills:** brand, design-system, ui-styling\n**Related Skills:** frontend-design, ui-ux-pro-max, ai-multimodal, chrome-devtools\n\n\nARGUMENTS: design logo for \"Nexo\" — VPN / secure connection service; strict, corporate, minimal; symbol of connection/link; generate via Gemini (user asked for the Gemini 2.5 logo generator)\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/Sagenkazaran/Library/Application Support/Claude/scratch-workspaces/f907b165-4712-485f-a44b-7f7d54b74cf9/77d6453f-aaee-4ad3-a7ea-34b17cbaf2e5/scratch-2026-10-26-b13584","sessionId":"1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"deep-singing-taco"}
