{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb","hash":"e6cd989b0e9fbf05f13ffa783b9d6796c451d5349b48e796e9ea54849e9f3b66","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QvBaAtzjkkF4v3ektWiQuw","name":"mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan","input":{"items":[{"content":"Pick an open-source base for Nexo app","status":"in_progress"},{"content":"Check build tools and disk on Mac","status":"pending"},{"content":"Rebrand: Nexo name, logo, colors","status":"pending"},{"content":"Simple Happ-like main screen","status":"pending"},{"content":"One-tap key import from web cabinet","status":"pending"},{"content":"Build and test Android APK","status":"pending"},{"content":"Build and test macOS app","status":"pending"},{"content":"Build Windows app","status":"pending"},{"content":"Add downloads to web cabinet","status":"pending"}],"scope":"continuation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015KCMs6sjnZomXeYC1MwxJr","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Evaluate fork base for VPN app","subagent_type":"general-purpose","prompt":"I need a factual recommendation for which open-source VPN client to fork into our own branded app \"Nexo\" for Android, macOS and Windows (iOS optional later). Our servers use Xray VLESS + Reality (vless://...reality links) and we serve a standard subscription URL (base64 list of vless:// links) over HTTPS. The goal: a very simple, beautiful app similar in UX to Happ (one big connect button, auto server selection, country list, subscription auto-imported by a deep link or by pasting a link), with our own name and logo, distributed outside stores (APK download, .dmg, .exe installer).\n\nResearch these candidates on GitHub and in their docs (read the actual LICENSE files and build docs, don't guess):\n1. Hiddify app (github.com/hiddify/hiddify-app) + hiddify-core\n2. Karing (github.com/KaringX/karing) — check whether ALL code needed to build is public (any private/closed packages, prebuilt binaries only?)\n3. sing-box official clients: sing-box-for-android (SFA, Kotlin) and sing-box for Apple (SFM/SFI); and whether sing-box core supports VLESS Reality (yes/no + version)\n4. Any other good multi-platform Flutter/Tauri client with permissive or GPL license that supports VLESS Reality (e.g. v2rayN is Windows-only C#, Throne/nekoray, GUI.for.SingBox, FlClash (Clash Meta/mihomo — check VLESS Reality support)).\n\nFor each, report: license (exact, plus any extra clauses like name/branding restrictions or non-commercial terms — commercial use matters, we sell subscriptions); can it be legally rebranded and sold as part of a paid service; platforms supported; is the full source buildable by us (list steps/tools: Flutter version, Go, gomobile, NDK, etc.); approximate complexity of the codebase; whether desktop uses TUN (admin rights) or system proxy; whether macOS build needs Apple Developer signing to run (Network Extension vs plain binary); whether a Windows build can be produced from GitHub Actions without a Windows PC; how actively maintained (last release date).\n\nFinish with a clear single recommendation for the base and a short list of the main risks. Keep the report under ~700 words. Include source URLs.","run_in_background":"true"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QEGR45NctwE5iJ6XBb3VCe","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"df -h / | tail -1; which flutter dart go java gh xcodebuild 2>&1; xcodebuild -version 2>&1 | head -1; ls ~/Library/Android/sdk 2>&1 | head; ls -d ~/flutter ~/development/flutter /opt/homebrew/bin/flutter 2>&1; sw_vers -productVersion; uname -m; gh auth status 2>&1 | head -3","description":"Check disk space and build tools on Mac"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
