{"parentUuid":"85f8f2a9-fad1-41f4-9756-1ab28eef9979","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgeZwxEJhrWq9w2ip5cQn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Skw2U8USw2EnW8vS2dHpvB","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"C=/private/tmp/claude-501/REDACTED/1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb/scratchpad/codex; cd ~/Projects/nexo-app && git pull -q origin main && git worktree add -q ../nexo-app-mac -b nexo/mac-universal && cat > $C/mac.md <<'EOF'\n# Task: build a universal (Apple Silicon + Intel) macOS app on an Intel GitHub runner\n\nRepo: github.com/Shahen777/nexo-app (Nexo, a GPL fork of FlClash: Flutter 3.47.6 + Go mihomo core \"FlClashCore\" +\nRust plugin `plugins/rust_api`). Our CI workflow is `.github/workflows/nexo.yaml` (job matrix android / macos /\nwindows; macOS builds run `dart setup.dart macos --env stable -v` on the runner). Free GitHub Apple Silicon runners\n(macos-15/macos-26 arm64) queue for hours and get cancelled, while `macos-15-intel` (Xcode 26) starts right away.\nGoal: produce ONE macOS .dmg from the `macos-15-intel` runner whose app runs natively on Apple Silicon and Intel\n(universal binaries), so we no longer depend on arm64 runners. The macOS 26 SDK (Xcode 26) is required\n(NSGlassEffectView), so do not target older images.\n\nWhat upstream does today (verify yourself):\n- `macos/Runner/Configs/Release.xcconfig` forces ARCHS to the host slice (FLCLASH_HOST_ARCH_*).\n- `plugins/setup/setup_hooks/lib/src/core_builder.dart` (~:115) skips non-host macOS slices\n  (\"Skipping non-host macOS slice\"); `_hostArchitecture` is injectable for tests.\n- `go_builder.dart` builds the Go core per target into libclash/macos/FlClashCore; the Xcode \"copy core\" run-script\n  phase in `macos/Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj` (~:371) checks with `lipo -archs` that the core has every ARCHS\n  slice.\n- `plugins/rust_api` is built through Dart native-assets hooks for the target architecture.\n\nDesign it so that when env `NEXO_MAC_UNIVERSAL=1` is set: ARCHS = arm64 x86_64; the Go core is built for both\ndarwin/arm64 and darwin/amd64 (Go cross-compiles; check whether the core uses cgo and set CC/CGO_CFLAGS with\n`-arch` / `-target` accordingly) and merged with `lipo -create` into the single FlClashCore the run-script expects,\nwithout the two slice builds overwriting each other; the Rust plugin builds both slices (add\n`rustup target add aarch64-apple-darwin x86_64-apple-darwin` to CI) and ends up universal. Without the env var,\nbehaviour stays exactly as upstream (host slice only) so upstream tests keep passing. Update or add unit tests in\n`plugins/setup/setup_hooks/test` for the new branch if that package has tests for core_builder.\nThen in `.github/workflows/nexo.yaml`: replace the two arm64 macOS matrix entries (macos-26, macos-15) and the\nmacos-15-intel entry with a single macOS entry on `macos-15-intel` that sets `NEXO_MAC_UNIVERSAL: '1'`, add the\nrustup targets step for macOS, and add a verification step after Build that mounts the produced dmg (in ./dist) and\nfails unless `lipo -archs` of Contents/MacOS/Nexo and Contents/MacOS/FlClashCore both list arm64 and x86_64.\nArtifact name: `nexo-macos-universal`.\n\nFlutter/Dart/Go/Xcode are NOT installed here — reason carefully from the code; CI will verify. Follow AGENTS.md\nstyle (ignore its commit-trailer rule). Do NOT commit or push. Keep dart-format style (2 spaces, trailing commas).\nReport briefly: files changed, how each slice is produced and merged, and what you are unsure will work in CI.\nEOF\ncodex exec -m gpt-6.1-terra -s workspace-write -C ~/Projects/nexo-app-mac -o $C/mac-report.md - < $C/mac.md > $C/mac.log 2>&1 &\necho launched","description":"Start Codex agent for a universal Mac build"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1229,"cache_read_input_tokens":282297,"output_tokens":2491,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":786},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1229,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2491,"cache_read_input_tokens":282297,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1229,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1229},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Skw2U8USw2EnW8vS2dHpvB":{"command":"C=/private/tmp/claude-501/REDACTED/1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb/scratchpad/codex; cd ~/Projects/nexo-app && git pull -q origin main && git worktree add -q ../nexo-app-mac -b nexo/mac-universal && cat > $C/mac.md <<'EOF'\n# Task: build a universal (Apple Silicon + Intel) macOS app on an Intel GitHub runner\n\nRepo: github.com/Shahen777/nexo-app (Nexo, a GPL fork of FlClash: Flutter 3.47.6 + Go mihomo core \"FlClashCore\" +\nRust plugin `plugins/rust_api`). Our CI workflow is `.github/workflows/nexo.yaml` (job matrix android / macos /\nwindows; macOS builds run `dart setup.dart macos --env stable -v` on the runner). Free GitHub Apple Silicon runners\n(macos-15/macos-26 arm64) queue for hours and get cancelled, while `macos-15-intel` (Xcode 26) starts right away.\nGoal: produce ONE macOS .dmg from the `macos-15-intel` runner whose app runs natively on Apple Silicon and Intel\n(universal binaries), so we no longer depend on arm64 runners. The macOS 26 SDK (Xcode 26) is required\n(NSGlassEffectView), so do not target older images.\n\nWhat upstream does today (verify yourself):\n- `macos/Runner/Configs/Release.xcconfig` forces ARCHS to the host slice (FLCLASH_HOST_ARCH_*).\n- `plugins/setup/setup_hooks/lib/src/core_builder.dart` (~:115) skips non-host macOS slices\n  (\"Skipping non-host macOS slice\"); `_hostArchitecture` is injectable for tests.\n- `go_builder.dart` builds the Go core per target into libclash/macos/FlClashCore; the Xcode \"copy core\" run-script\n  phase in `macos/Runner.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj` (~:371) checks with `lipo -archs` that the core has every ARCHS\n  slice.\n- `plugins/rust_api` is built through Dart native-assets hooks for the target architecture.\n\nDesign it so that when env `NEXO_MAC_UNIVERSAL=1` is set: ARCHS = arm64 x86_64; the Go core is built for both\ndarwin/arm64 and darwin/amd64 (Go cross-compiles; check whether the core uses cgo and set CC/CGO_CFLAGS with\n`-arch` / `-target` accordingly) and merged with `lipo -create` into the single FlClashCore the run-script expects,\nwithout the two slice builds overwriting each other; the Rust plugin builds both slices (add\n`rustup target add aarch64-apple-darwin x86_64-apple-darwin` to CI) and ends up universal. Without the env var,\nbehaviour stays exactly as upstream (host slice only) so upstream tests keep passing. Update or add unit tests in\n`plugins/setup/setup_hooks/test` for the new branch if that package has tests for core_builder.\nThen in `.github/workflows/nexo.yaml`: replace the two arm64 macOS matrix entries (macos-26, macos-15) and the\nmacos-15-intel entry with a single macOS entry on `macos-15-intel` that sets `NEXO_MAC_UNIVERSAL: '1'`, add the\nrustup targets step for macOS, and add a verification step after Build that mounts the produced dmg (in ./dist) and\nfails unless `lipo -archs` of Contents/MacOS/Nexo and Contents/MacOS/FlClashCore both list arm64 and x86_64.\nArtifact name: `nexo-macos-universal`.\n\nFlutter/Dart/Go/Xcode are NOT installed here — reason carefully from the code; CI will verify. Follow AGENTS.md\nstyle (ignore its commit-trailer rule). Do NOT commit or push. Keep dart-format style (2 spaces, trailing commas).\nReport briefly: files changed, how each slice is produced and merged, and what you are unsure will work in CI.\nEOF\ncodex exec -m gpt-6.1-terra -s workspace-write -C ~/Projects/nexo-app-mac -o $C/mac-report.md - < $C/mac.md > $C/mac.log 2>&1 &\necho launched","description":"Start Codex agent for a universal Mac build"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"27f683b7-cd9c-461e-92e4-fa2e5d9af75f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgeZwwvwpChjRz6onKghK","requestRef":"e7a93f04-9d53-4c1d-8ef7-24d88184507b","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e6443bcc-3405-47da-b26a-f34abbc6b6be","timestamp":"2026-11-02T18:24:22.108Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/Sagenkazaran/Library/Application Support/Claude/scratch-workspaces/f907b165-4712-485f-a44b-7f7d54b74cf9/77d6453f-aaee-4ad3-a7ea-34b17cbaf2e5/scratch-2026-10-26-b13584","sessionId":"1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"deep-singing-taco"}
