 {'User-Agent': browserUa}));\n    _clashDio = Dio();\n    _clashDio.httpClientAdapter = IOHttpClientAdapter(\n      createHttpClient: () {\n        final client = HttpClient();\n        client.findProxy = (Uri uri) {\n          client.userAgent = globalState.ua;\n          final read = _read;\n          if (read == null) {\n            return 'DIRECT';\n          }\n          return FlClashHttpOverrides.findProxyForReader(read, uri);\n        };\n        return client;\n      },\n    );\n  }\n\n  Future<Response<T>> _download<T>(String url, ResponseType responseType) {\n    final target = downloadTarget(url);\n    final cancelToken = CancelToken();\n    return _clashDio\n        .getUri<T>(\n          target.uri,\n          options: Options(responseType: responseType, headers: target.headers),\n          cancelToken: cancelToken,\n        )\n        .timeout(\n          downloadTimeoutDuration,\n          onTimeout: () {\n            cancelToken.cancel();\n            throw DioException.receiveTimeout(\n              timeout: downloadTimeoutDuration,\n              requestOptions: RequestOptions(path: url),\n            );\n          },\n        );\n  }\n\n  Future<Response<Uint8List>> getFileResponseForUrl(String url) async {\n    try {\n      return await _download<Uint8List>(url, ResponseType.bytes);\n    } catch (e) {\n      commonPrint.log(\n        'getFileResponseForUrl error ${compactError(e)}',\n        logLevel: LogLevel.warning,\n      );\n      rethrow;\n    }\n  }\n\n  Future<Response<String>> getTextResponseForUrl(String url) async {\n    try {\n      return await _download<String>(url, ResponseType.plain);\n    } catch (e) {\n      commonPrint.log(\n        'getTextResponseForUrl error ${compactError(e)}',\n        logLevel: LogLevel.warning,\n      );\n      rethrow;\n    }\n  }\n\n  /// Null when this build is current; throws when GitHub cannot be asked.\n  Future<Map<String, dynamic>?> checkForUpdate() async {\n    final release = await latestRelease();\n    final remoteVersion = release['tag_name'] as String;\n    final version = globalState.packageInfo.version;\n    final hasUpdate =\n        compareVersions(remoteVersion.replaceAll('v', ''), version) > 0;\n    return hasUpdate ? release : null;\n  }\n\n  /// The release page redirect still answers once the hourly API quota is spent.\n  @visibleForTesting\n  Future<Map<String, dynamic>> latestRelease() async {\n    try {\n      final response = await dio.get<Map<String, dynamic>>(\n        'https://api.github.com/repos/$repository/releases/latest',\n        options: Options(responseType: ResponseType.json),\n      );\n      return response.data!;\n    } on DioException catch (error) {\n      commonPrint.log(\n        'latest release API failed: ${compactError(error)}',\n        logLevel: LogLevel.warning,\n      );\n    }\n    final response = await dio.get<void>(\n      'https://github.com/$repository/releases/latest',\n      options: Options(\n        followRedirects: false,\n        validateStatus: (status) => status != null && status < 400,\n      ),\n    );\n    final location = response.headers.value(HttpHeaders.locationHeader);\n    final segments = Uri.tryParse(location ?? '')?.pathSegments ?? const [];\n    final tagIndex = segments.indexOf('tag') + 1;\n    if (tagIndex == 0 || tagIndex >= segments.length) {\n      throw FormatException('No release tag in the redirect', location);\n    }\n    return {'tag_name': segments[tagIndex]};\n  }\n}\n\nfinal request = Request();\n\n/// Some subscription servers send a gzip or zlib body without saying so in\n/// Content-Encoding, which is the only signal dart:io decompresses on.\nUint8List decompressUnlabeled(Uint8List bytes) {\n  final codec = switch (bytes) {\n    [0x1f, 0x8b, ...] => gzip,\n    [0x78, final flags, ...] when (0x78 << 8 | flags) % 31 == 0 => zlib,\n    _ => null,\n  };\n  if (codec == null) {\n    return bytes;\n  }\n  try {\n    return Uint8List.fromList(codec.decode(bytes));\n  } on FormatException {\n    return bytes;\n  }\n}\n\n/// dart:io turns [Uri.userInfo] into Basic credentials still percent-encoded.\n@visibleForTesting\n({Uri uri, Map<String, Object> headers}) downloadTarget(String url) {\n  final uri = url.webUri ?? Uri.parse(url);\n  if (uri.userInfo.isEmpty) {\n    return (uri: uri, headers: const {});\n  }\n  final credentials = uri.userInfo.split(':').map(_decodeUserInfo).join(':');\n  return (\n    uri: uri.replace(userInfo: ''),\n    headers: {\n      HttpHeaders.authorizationHeader:\n          'Basic ${base64.encode(utf8.encode(credentials))}',\n    },\n  );\n}\n\nString _decodeUserInfo(String value) {\n  try {\n    return Uri.decodeComponent(value);\n  } on ArgumentError {\n    return value;\n  }\n}\n\nString? getFileNameForDisposition(String? disposition) {\n  if (disposition == null) return null;\n  final parseValue = HeaderValue.parse(disposition);\n  final parameters = parseValue.parameters;\n  final fileNamePointKey = parameters.keys.firstWhere(\n    (key) => key == 'filename*',\n    orElse: () => '',\n  );\n  if (fileNamePointKey.isNotEmpty) {\n    final res = parameters[fileNamePointKey]?.split(\"''\") ?? [];\n    if (res.length >= 2) {\n      return Uri.decodeComponent(res[1]);\n    }\n  }\n  final fileNameKey = parameters.keys.firstWhere(\n    (key) => key == 'filename',\n    orElse: () => '',\n  );\n  if (fileNameKey.isEmpty) return null;\n  return parameters[fileNameKey];\n}\n---\nimport 'dart:async';\n\nimport 'package:fl_clash/common/common.dart';\nimport 'package:fl_clash/enum/enum.dart';\nimport 'package:fl_clash/providers/providers.dart';\nimport 'package:fl_clash/state.dart';\nimport 'package:fl_clash/ui/icons/icons.dart';\nimport 'package:fl_clash/ui/ui.dart';\nimport 'package:material_ui/material_ui.dart';\nimport 'package:flutter_riverpod/flutter_riverpod.dart';\n\n@immutable\nclass Contributor {\n  final String avatar;\n  final String name;\n\n  const Contributor({required this.avatar, required this.name});\n}\n\nclass AboutView extends ConsumerWidget {\n  const AboutView({super.key});\n\n  static const _contributors = [\n    Contributor(avatar: 'assets/images/avatar/june2.jpg', name: 'June2'),\n    Contributor(avatar: 'assets/images/avatar/arue.jpg', name: 'Arue'),\n  ];\n\n  Future<void> _checkUpdate(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) async {\n    if (ref.read(loadingProvider(LoadingTag.checkUpdate))) return;\n    final commonAction = ref.read(commonActionProvider.notifier);\n    final result = await globalState.loadingRun(\n      () async => (release: await request.checkForUpdate()),\n      title: context.appLocalizations.checkUpdate,\n      tag: LoadingTag.checkUpdate,\n    );\n    if (result == null) return;\n    unawaited(\n      commonAction.checkUpdateResultHandle(data: result.release, isUser: true),\n    );\n  }\n\n  Widget _buildLinkItem({\n    required Glyph glyph,\n    required String title,\n    required String url,\n    required String label,\n  }) {\n    return ListItem(\n      leading: _LinkBadge(glyph: glyph),\n      title: Text(title),\n      subtitle: Text(label, maxLines: 1, overflow: TextOverflow.ellipsis),\n      trailing: const GlyphIcon(AppGlyphs.openExternal),\n      onTap: () {\n        dialogs.openUrl(url);\n      },\n    );\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context, WidgetRef ref) {\n    final appLocalizations = context.appLocalizations;\n    final isLoading = ref.watch(loadingProvider(LoadingTag.checkUpdate));\n    return CommonScaffold(\n      isLoading: isLoading,\n      title: appLocalizations.about,\n      body: ListView(\n        padding: const EdgeInsets.symmetric(horizontal: 16).copyWith(\n          top: context.contentTopPadding,\n          bottom: 32 + context.bottomInset,\n        ),\n        children: [\n          _AboutHero(\n            isCheckingUpdate: isLoading,\n            onCheckUpdate: () {\n              _checkUpdate(context, ref);\n            },\n            onEnterDeveloperMode: () {\n              ref\n                  .read(appSettingProvider.notifier)\n                  .update((state) => state.copyWith(developerMode: true));\n              context.showNotifier(\n                appLocalizations.developerModeEnableTip,\n                level: MessageLevel.success,\n              );\n            },\n          ),\n          const SizedBox(height: 8),\n          generateSection(\n            title: appLocalizations.more,\n            items: [\n              _buildLinkItem(\n                glyph: AppGlyphs.code,\n                title: appLocalizations.project,\n                url: 'https://github.com/$repository',\n                label: 'github.com/$repository',\n              ),\n              _buildLinkItem(\n                glyph: AppGlyphs.code,\n                title: appLocalizations.basedOnFlClash,\n                url: 'https://github.com/chen08209/FlClash',\n                label: 'github.com/chen08209/FlClash',\n              ),\n              _buildLinkItem(\n                glyph: AppGlyphs.cpu,\n                title: appLocalizations.core,\n                url: 'https://github.com/chen08209/Clash.Meta/tree/FlClash',\n                label: 'github.com/chen08209/Clash.Meta',\n              ),\n              _buildLinkItem(\n                glyph: AppGlyphs.send,\n                title: 'Telegram',\n                url: 'https://t.me/FlClash',\n                label: 't.me/FlClash',\n              ),\n            ],\n          ),\n          generateSection(\n            title: appLocalizations.otherContributors,\n            items: [\n              for (final contributor in _contributors)\n                ListItem(\n                  leading: CircleAvatar(\n                    foregroundImage: AssetImage(contributor.avatar),\n                  ),\n                  title: Text(contributor.name),\n                  subtitle: Text(appLocalizations.appIconDesign),\n                ),\n            ],\n          ),\n        ],\n      ),\n    );\n  }\n}\n\nclass _AboutHero extends StatelessWidget {\n  final bool isCheckingUpdate;\n  final VoidCallback onCheckUpdate;\n  final VoidCallback onEnterDeveloperMode;\n\n  const _AboutHero({\n    required this.isCheckingUpdate,\n    required this.onCheckUpdate,\n    required this.onEnterDeveloperMode,\n  });\n\n  static const _logoSize = 96.0;\n  static const _logoInset = 14.0;\n\n  @override\n  Widget build(BuildContext context) {\n    final colorScheme = context.colorScheme;\n    final appLocalizations = context.appLocalizations;\n    return Padding(\n      padding: const EdgeInsets.fromLTRB(24, 16, 24, 0),\n      child: Column(\n        children: [\n          _DeveloperModeDetector(\n            onEnterDeveloperMode: onEnterDeveloperMode,\n            child: DecoratedBox(\n---\nandroid/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml:85:                <action android:name=\"${applicationId}.action.START\" />\nandroid/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml:89:                <action android:name=\"${applicationId}.action.STOP\" />\nandroid/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml:93:                <action android:name=\"${applicationId}.action.TOGGLE\" />\nandroid/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml:115:            android:permission=\"${applicationId}.permission.RECEIVE_BROADCASTS\">\nandroid/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml:117:                <action android:name=\"${applicationId}.intent.action.VPN_START_REQUESTED\" />\nandroid/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml:118:                <action android:name=\"${applicationId}.intent.action.VPN_REVOKED\" />\nandroid/app/build.gradle.kts:36:        applicationId = \"app.nexo.vpn\"\nandroid/app/build.gradle.kts:39:        versionCode = flutter.versionCode\nandroid/app/build.gradle.kts:40:        versionName = flutter.versionName\nandroid/app/build.gradle.kts:63:            applicationIdSuffix = \".dev\"\nandroid/app/build.gradle.kts:73:                applicationIdSuffix = \".dev\"\nExt.kt\nFlClashApplication.kt\nMainActivity.kt\nQuickActionActivity.kt\nServiceBroadcastReceiver.kt\nServiceController.kt\nServiceState.kt\nServiceStateHost.kt\nServiceStateMachine.kt\nTileService.kt\nmodels\npackages\nplugins\nclash\n# AGENTS.md\n\nThis file is the entry point for AI coding agents working in this repository. Keep it small: detailed guidance lives under\n`.agents/`, and discoverable repo skills live under `.agents/skills/*/SKILL.md`.\n\n## Start Here\n\nRead these files before making changes:\n\n- [.agents/project.md](.agents/project.md): project overview, versions, and build dependencies.\n- [.agents/commands.md](.agents/commands.md): build, development, code generation, and test commands.\n- [.agents/rules.md](.agents/rules.md): lint, testing, generated-code, and workflow rules.\n\nRead these only when the task touches their area:\n\n- [.agents/architecture.md](.agents/architecture.md): core integration, providers, database, managers, build system, and\n  local plugins.\n- [.agents/setting-changes.md](.agents/setting-changes.md): whether a changed setting is patched live, re-applies the\n  profile, or asks for an Android VPN restart.\n- [.agents/surfaces.md](.agents/surfaces.md): fill levels, selection and status colors, and the few borders that\n  remain, for any change to how a surface is colored.\n- [.agents/agent-config.md](.agents/agent-config.md): how to choose between `AGENTS.md`, `.agents`, skills, Codex config,\n  command rules, and hooks.\n- [.agents/worktrees.md](.agents/worktrees.md): worktree hygiene across Claude Code, Codex, and Gemini.\n- [.agents/flutter-upgrade.md](.agents/flutter-upgrade.md): SDK-pinned workarounds to recheck before changing the\n  Flutter version.\n- [.agents/skills.md](.agents/skills.md): index of repo-scoped skills in `.agents/skills/`.\n\n## Highest Priority Rules\n\n- When the user explicitly requests a scoped, low-risk change, inspect the relevant context and implement it directly.\n  Do not require brainstorming, design documents, implementation plans, multiple-option proposals, or repeated confirmation.\n  Ask only when material ambiguity, destructive impact, additional authority, or scope expansion could change the result.\n- The request sets the scope. A pre-existing bug, cleanup, or refactor the task did not ask for is a follow-up in the\n  summary, not part of the change. Edit a file surgically when a rewrite would give the same result, keep scratch checks\n  out of the repository, and commit tests only where the task asks for them or the neighbouring code already keeps them.\n- Comments are allowed and sometimes necessary; excess is the problem. A comment must carry something the code cannot\n  say — a non-obvious constraint, an upstream behavior being worked around, a reason a reader would otherwise get\n  wrong. Never restate what the code does, narrate the change you just made, record what the code used to be, or\n  annotate step by step; a block that seems to need a comment per line needs better names or a smaller decomposition.","is_error":false},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015c22VGkTey6unZA9hVxKg7","type":"tool_result","content":"    name = request.match_info.get(\"name\", \"\")\n    allowed = {v for apps in catalog.VIDEOS.values() for v in apps.values()}\n    path = os.path.join(ASSETS, \"video\", name)\n    if name not in allowed or not os.path.exists(path):\n        raise web.HTTPNotFound(text=\"Not found\")\n    return web.FileResponse(path, headers={\"Cache-Control\": \"public, max-age=86400\"})\n\n\nasync def handle_download(request):\n    \"\"\"Nexo app installers (assets/downloads/, kept out of git).\"\"\"\n    name = request.match_info.get(\"name\", \"\")\n    path = os.path.join(ASSETS, \"downloads\", name)\n    if name not in catalog.NEXO_FILES or not os.path.exists(path):\n        raise web.HTTPNotFound(text=\"Not found\")\n    return web.FileResponse(path, headers={\"Content-Type\": catalog.NEXO_FILES[name], \"Cache-Control\": \"no-cache\",\n                                           \"Content-Disposition\": f'attachment; filename=\"{name}\"'})\n\n\nWEB_FILES = (\"icon.png\", \"karing-poster.jpg\")\n\n\nasync def handle_web_file(request):\n    name = request.match_info.get(\"name\", \"\")\n    path = os.path.join(ASSETS, \"web\", name)\n    if name not in WEB_FILES or not os.path.exists(path):\n        raise web.HTTPNotFound(text=\"Not found\")\n    return web.FileResponse(path, headers={\"Cache-Control\": \"public, max-age=604800\"})\n\n\nasync def handle_font(request):\n    name = request.match_info.get(\"name\", \"\")\n    path = os.path.join(ASSETS, \"web\", \"fonts\", name)\n    if not name.endswith(\".woff2\") or \"/\" in name or not os.path.exists(path):\n        raise web.HTTPNotFound(text=\"Not found\")\n    return web.FileResponse(path, headers={\"Cache-Control\": \"public, max-age=31536000, immutable\"})\n\n\nasync def handle_manifest(_request):\n    return web.json_response({\"name\": BRAND_TITLE, \"short_name\": BRAND_TITLE, \"start_url\": \"/app\", \"display\": \"standalone\",\n                              \"background_color\": \"#2F6BFF\", \"theme_color\": \"#2F6BFF\",\n                              \"icons\": [{\"src\": \"/web/icon.png\", \"sizes\": \"512x512\", \"type\": \"image/png\"}]},\n                             content_type=\"application/manifest+json\")\n\n\ndef add_routes(app):\n    app.router.add_get(\"/app\", handle_landing)\n    app.router.add_post(\"/app/start\", handle_start)\n    app.router.add_get(\"/app/restore\", handle_restore_form)\n    app.router.add_post(\"/app/restore\", handle_restore)\n    app.router.add_get(\"/c/{token}\", handle_cabinet)\n    app.router.add_post(\"/c/{token}/device\", handle_device)\n    app.router.add_post(\"/c/{token}/pay\", handle_pay)\n    app.router.add_post(\"/c/{token}/telegram\", handle_telegram)\n    app.router.add_get(\"/docs/{name}\", handle_doc)\n    app.router.add_get(\"/media/{name}\", handle_media)\n    app.router.add_get(\"/nexo/download/{name}\", handle_download)\n    app.router.add_get(\"/web/manifest.webmanifest\", handle_manifest)\n    app.router.add_get(\"/web/fonts/{name}\", handle_font)\n    app.router.add_get(\"/web/{name}\", handle_web_file)\n3b92593ad74c5543a6a01fa95337c8db2247c86e34d83fdb0d587b6525087fa7  /opt/nexo-bot/assets/downloads/Nexo-android.apk\nList of devices attached\n63311JEA320837\tdevice\n\n    versionCode=2026104401 minSdk=24 targetSdk=37\n    versionName=0.9.2","is_error":false}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb","hash":"4a0d0ff4c94eab30572a20b6746740a9971516cce2bfd850ac15d0057eef80f6","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015PUVVQzRQtG8AMSWsJd64j","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/Sagenkazaran/Projects/nexo-app && sed -n 80,100p lib/providers/actions/common.dart; sed -n 140,200p lib/providers/actions/common.dart; echo --- ; cat .agents/commands.md | head -60; echo ---; cat .agents/rules.md | head -50; echo ---; ls .github/workflows 2>/dev/null; which flutter dart; flutter --version 2>/dev/null | head -2; ls android/app/*.jks android/*.properties android/key* 2>/dev/null; git check-ignore android/local.properties android/key.properties; sed -n 40,62p android/app/build.gradle.kts; echo ---; ls ~/Projects/nexo-app/build/app/outputs/flutter-apk 2>/dev/null | head; grep -n 'Permission\\|uses-permission' android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml | head -30; sed -n 100,135p android/app/src/main/AndroidManifest.xml; cat android/app/src/main/kotlin/com/follow/clash/MainActivity.kt 2>/dev/null | head -5; find android -name MainActivity.kt; ls android/app/src/main/kotlin/*/*/*/plugins 2>/dev/null; grep -n -E 'NEXO_FILES' -A8 /dev/null","description":"Read update handler, build rules, CI and Android plugin layout"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UMRrjGAWww3a1rPniX2p9T","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"ssh -i ~/.ssh/codex_aura_vps codex-aura@152.53.50.204 'grep -n -E \"NEXO_FILES|PUBLIC_BASE|nexo/download\" -A6 /opt/nexo-bot/catalog.py | head -30; grep -n \"PUBLIC_BASE_URL\" /opt/nexo-bot/*.py | head -5'; curl -s -o /dev/null -w 'github repo status %{http_code}\\n' -m 10 https://api.github.com/repos/Shahen777/nexo-app/releases/latest; gh run list --repo Shahen777/nexo-app -L 5 2>&1 | head -8; gh release list --repo Shahen777/nexo-app -L 3 2>&1 | head -5","description":"Check download catalog, public address and GitHub release availability"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb","hash":"3f42bebadaed14be1944a90810c6ee15249ca3264bcf564de86acf7ddd467271","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015PUVVQzRQtG8AMSWsJd64j","type":"tool_result","content":"      );\n      return null;\n    }\n  }\n\n  Future<bool> autoCheckUpdate() async {\n    if (!ref.read(appSettingProvider).autoCheckUpdate) return false;\n    final Map<String, dynamic>? res;\n    try {\n      res = await request.checkForUpdate();\n    } catch (error) {\n      commonPrint.log(\n        'checkForUpdate failed: ${compactError(error)}',\n        logLevel: LogLevel.warning,\n      );\n      return false;\n    }\n    await checkUpdateResultHandle(data: res);\n    return res != null;\n  }\n\n          ),\n      ],\n    ];\n  }\n\n  Future<void> checkUpdateResultHandle({\n    Map<String, dynamic>? data,\n    bool isUser = false,\n  }) async {\n    if (data != null) {\n      final context = globalState.navigatorKey.currentContext!;\n      final res = await dialogs.showMessage(\n        title: currentAppLocalizations.discoverNewVersion,\n        message: _releaseSpan(\n          context,\n          data['tag_name'] as String,\n          data['body'] as String?,\n        ),\n        confirmText: currentAppLocalizations.goDownload,\n        cancelText: isUser ? null : currentAppLocalizations.noLongerRemind,\n      );\n      if (res == true) {\n        unawaited(\n          launchUrl(\n            Uri.parse('https://github.com/$repository/releases/latest'),\n          ),\n        );\n      } else if (!isUser && res == false) {\n        ref\n            .read(appSettingProvider.notifier)\n            .update((state) => state.copyWith(autoCheckUpdate: false));\n      }\n    } else if (isUser) {\n      unawaited(\n        dialogs.showAlert(\n          title: currentAppLocalizations.checkUpdate,\n          message: TextSpan(text: currentAppLocalizations.checkUpdateError),\n        ),\n      );\n    }\n  }\n}\n---\n# Commands\n\n## Building\n\nUpdate submodules first. The ClashMeta Go core lives in `core/Clash.Meta/`.\n\n```bash\ngit submodule update --init --recursive\n```\n\nFull package build, including Go core, Flutter, and packaging, runs through `setup.dart`:\n\n```bash\ndart setup.dart macos\ndart setup.dart linux\ndart setup.dart windows\ndart setup.dart android\n```\n\nThe desktop Go core and the Rust helper build automatically: Flutter runs\n`plugins/setup/hook/build.dart` on every `flutter build` and `flutter test`,\nand the hook drives `CoreBuilder` from the `setup_hooks` package in\n`plugins/setup/setup_hooks/`. Artifacts land in `libclash/`. Android's Core is\nthe AAR the `:core` Gradle module builds with `gomobile bind` before anything\ncompiles against it; that needs `go` on `PATH` and nothing else, since the\ngomobile tools come from `core/go.mod` and the NDK from AGP. The hook reruns only when Go, Rust, or\n`setup_hooks` inputs change; the fingerprint cache lives in\n`.dart_tool/setup_build_cache/`. To force a rebuild, delete that directory:\n\n```bash\nrm -rf .dart_tool/setup_build_cache\n```\n\nFlutter hides the hook's output on success, so to see why the Core was or was\nnot rebuilt read `.dart_tool/setup_build_cache/hook.log`; each invocation starts\nwith a `===` line carrying its timestamp and target.\n\nThe hook runs for `flutter test` and for `dart run` of any root-package script\ntoo, so a pure Dart test run needs the Go toolchain, and on Linux and Windows\nalso `cargo` and `rustc` — the Helper fingerprint shells out to both even on a\ncache hit. The hook protocol carries no build mode and no caller, so the only\nswitch is the user-define in the root `pubspec.yaml`:\n\n```yaml\nhooks:\n  user_defines:\n    setup:\n      build_assets: true   # false turns the Go core and Helper hook into a no-op\n    rust_api:\n      build_assets: true   # false does the same for the Rust library\n```\n\nCI flips `setup` to `false` with `yq` in its throwaway checkout before\n`dart run tool/changelog.dart` and `dart run tool/test.dart`; no test loads the Go core. `rust_api`\nstays on there because the editor tests in `test/plugins/code_forge/` and the socket\ntest in `test/core/desktop/ipc_native_test.dart` load the Rust library the hook\nbuilds; the release-notes job, which runs no tests, flips both.\nNever commit `false`: a build with it set stages whatever `libclash/` already\nholds and bundles no Rust library, which is why `setup.dart` refuses to package\nwhile it is set. Locally, `false` is worth setting for a Dart-only test loop,\n---\n# Rules\n\nThese are repository coding and testing conventions. Codex command permission rules belong in `.codex/rules/*.rules`; see `.agents/agent-config.md` before adding those.\n\n## Dart and Flutter Style\n\nThe lint set lives in `lint_options.yaml` at the repo root. The root `analysis_options.yaml` and every local plugin under\n`plugins/*` include it, so application and plugin code are held to the same rules. Add or change a rule there, not in an\nindividual `analysis_options.yaml`; those files carry only their own `analyzer.exclude` entries.\n\n`lint_options.yaml` enforces these non-default rules:\n\n- `prefer_single_quotes: true`: always use single quotes.\n- `require_trailing_commas: true`: use trailing commas in multi-line argument lists.\n- `sort_child_properties_last: true`: `child:` must be the last named parameter.\n- `avoid_print: true`: do not use `print()` calls.\n- `prefer_const_constructors: true` and `prefer_const_declarations: true`.\n- `prefer_final_locals: true` and `prefer_final_in_for_each: true`.\n- `always_declare_return_types: true`.\n- `only_throw_errors: true`: throw an `Exception` or `Error`, never a bare `String`.\n\nFailures whose whole content is a message meant for the user throw\n`MessageException` from `lib/common/exception.dart`. Its `toString()` is the bare\nmessage, which is what `globalState.safeRun` surfaces in the dialog, and the\nthrow stays catchable as an `Exception` and carries a stack trace. Assert on it\nwith `isA<MessageException>().having((e) => e.message, 'message', ...)`, not on a\nraw string.\n\n### Corner Radius\n\nRounded corners are superellipses (continuous corners) everywhere, never circular arcs; when a component offers\nboth, pick the superellipse. `test/lint/superellipse_corners_test.dart` fails on the circular APIs below in `lib/`. Use\nthe superellipse API at each layer:\n\n- Shapes: `RoundedSuperellipseBorder` instead of `RoundedRectangleBorder`.\n- Clips: `ClipRSuperellipse` instead of `ClipRRect`.\n- Container decorations: `ShapeDecoration(shape: RoundedSuperellipseBorder(...))` instead of\n  `BoxDecoration(borderRadius: ...)`; borders move to the shape's `side`, and a `Container` with\n  `clipBehavior` still clips to the shape path.\n- Canvas: `canvas.drawRSuperellipse(RSuperellipse.fromRectAndRadius(...))` instead of `drawRRect`.\n- Ink: `InkWell.customBorder` with an `AppShape` instead of `InkWell.borderRadius`.\n\nPassing `BorderRadius.circular(x)` as the `borderRadius` argument of these APIs is expected — it only\ncarries the corner magnitude; the rendered geometry stays a superellipse.\n\nPills are no exception. `StadiumBorder` joins its round caps to the straight sides with a curvature jump, while\n`AppShape.full`, a superellipse at full radius, blends them, and on a square it renders the exact circle, so it serves\ncircles too. Material 3 defaults every button, icon button, segmented button, and search bar to `StadiumBorder`;\n`ThemeData.withAppShapes` replaces that for the button themes, and a local `FilledButtonTheme` or `IconButtonTheme`\nreplaces the app's, so merge the ambient `XButtonTheme.of(context).style` into it, as `CommonMinFilledButtonTheme`\n---\nbuild.yaml\nnexo-format.yaml\nnexo.yaml\npages.yaml\nandroid/gradle.properties\nandroid/local.properties\nandroid/key.properties\n        versionName = flutter.versionName\n    }\n\n    signingConfigs {\n        if (hasReleaseSigning) {\n            create(\"release\") {\n                storeFile = releaseStoreFile\n                storePassword = REDACTED\n                keyAlias = releaseKeyAlias\n                keyPassword = REDACTED\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    packaging {\n        jniLibs {\n            useLegacyPackaging = true\n        }\n    }\n\n    buildTypes {\n        debug {\n            isMinifyEnabled = false\n---\n18:    <uses-permission android:name=\"android.permission.INTERNET\" />\n19:    <uses-permission android:name=\"android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE\" />\n20:    <uses-permission android:name=\"android.permission.ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE\" />\n21:    <uses-permission android:name=\"android.permission.ACCESS_WIFI_STATE\" />\n22:    <uses-permission android:name=\"android.permission.CHANGE_NETWORK_STATE\" />\n23:    <uses-permission\n25:        tools:ignore=\"QueryAllPackagesPermission\" />\n26:    <uses-permission android:name=\"com.android.permission.GET_INSTALLED_APPS\" />\n27:    <uses-permission android:name=\"android.permission.FOREGROUND_SERVICE_SPECIAL_USE\" />\n28:    <uses-permission android:name=\"android.permission.POST_NOTIFICATIONS\" />\n29:    <uses-permission android:name=\"android.permission.REQUEST_IGNORE_BATTERY_OPTIMIZATIONS\" />\n30:    <uses-permission android:name=\"android.permission.ACCESS_LOCAL_NETWORK\" />\n            android:icon=\"@drawable/ic\"\n            android:label=\"@string/app_name\"\n            android:permission=\"android.permission.BIND_QUICK_SETTINGS_TILE\">\n            <intent-filter>\n                <action android:name=\"android.service.quicksettings.action.QS_TILE\" />\n            </intent-filter>\n            <meta-data\n                android:name=\"android.service.quicksettings.TOGGLEABLE_TILE\"\n                android:value=\"true\" />\n        </service>\n\n        <receiver\n            android:name=\".ServiceBroadcastReceiver\"\n            android:enabled=\"true\"\n            android:exported=\"true\"\n            android:permission=\"${applicationId}.permission.RECEIVE_BROADCASTS\">\n            <intent-filter>\n                <action android:name=\"${applicationId}.intent.action.VPN_START_REQUESTED\" />\n                <action android:name=\"${applicationId}.intent.action.VPN_REVOKED\" />\n            </intent-filter>\n        </receiver>\n\n        <meta-data\n            android:name=\"flutterEmbedding\"\n            android:value=\"2\" />\n    </application>\n</manifest>\npackage com.follow.clash\n\nimport com.follow.clash.plugins.AppPlugin\nimport com.follow.clash.plugins.BatteryPlugin\nimport com.follow.clash.plugins.ServicePlugin\nandroid/app/src/main/kotlin/com/follow/clash/MainActivity.kt\nAppPlugin.kt\nBatteryPlugin.kt\nServicePlugin.kt\nTilePlugin.kt","is_error":false},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UMRrjGAWww3a1rPniX2p9T","type":"tool_result","content":"13:from config import PUBLIC_BASE_URL\n14-\n15-HAPP_IOS = \"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/happ-proxy-utility/id6504287215?l=ru\"\n16-HAPP_SITE = \"https://www.happ.su/main\"\n17-HAPP_PLAY = \"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.happproxy\"\n18-HAPP_APK = \"https://github.com/Happ-proxy/happ-android/releases/latest/download/Happ.apk\"\n19-HAPP_TV_IOS = \"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/happ-proxy-utility-for-tv/id6748297274\"\n--\n26:NEXO_FILES = {\n27-    \"Nexo-android.apk\": \"application/vnd.android.package-archive\",\n28-    \"Nexo-android-old.apk\": \"application/vnd.android.package-archive\",\n29-    \"Nexo-windows-setup.exe\": \"application/vnd.microsoft.portable-executable\",\n30-    \"Nexo-macos.dmg\": \"application/x-apple-diskimage\",\n31-}\n32-\n--\n35:    return f\"{PUBLIC_BASE_URL.rstrip('/')}/nexo/download/{name}\"\n36-\n37-\n38-@dataclass(frozen=True)\n39-class App:\n40-    key: str\n41-    name: str\n/opt/nexo-bot/catalog.py:13:from config import PUBLIC_BASE_URL\n/opt/nexo-bot/catalog.py:35:    return f\"{PUBLIC_BASE_URL.rstrip('/')}/nexo/download/{name}\"\n/opt/nexo-bot/config.py:15:PUBLIC_BASE_URL = os.environ.get(\"AURA_PUBLIC_BASE_URL\", \"\")\n/opt/nexo-bot/subscription.py:27:PUBLIC_BASE_URL_KEY = web.AppKey(\"public_base_url\", str)\n/opt/nexo-bot/subscription.py:75:        \"isp-url\": request.app[PUBLIC_BASE_URL_KEY],\ngithub repo status 404\ncompleted\tsuccess\tnexo-build\tnexo-build\tmain\tworkflow_dispatch\t41662912143\t21m57s\t2026-11-03T15:20:48Z\ncompleted\tsuccess\tnexo-build\tnexo-build\tmain\tworkflow_dispatch\t41515574708\t31m3s\t2026-11-02T20:02:57Z\ncompleted\tfailure\tbuild\tbuild\tmain\tworkflow_dispatch\t41515570385\t15m3s\t2026-11-02T20:02:55Z\ncompleted\tsuccess\tnexo-format\tnexo-format\tmain\tworkflow_dispatch\t41515358385\t1m15s\t2026-11-02T20:01:33Z\ncompleted\tsuccess\tnexo-build\tnexo-build\tmain\tworkflow_dispatch\t41509146419\t27m10s\t2026-11-02T19:21:15Z","is_error":false}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb","hash":"4d7ac07802b2479ba69448be015dc0841faebac963c16ea289ef94632cf4f966","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LU22GstzeZeBgomtnxmavp","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/Sagenkazaran/Projects/nexo-app && cat .github/workflows/nexo.yaml; ls ~/flutter ~/fvm ~/development/flutter 2>/dev/null | head -5; ls /opt/homebrew/bin | grep -iE 'flutter|dart|fvm|^go$' ; cat lib/common/package.dart | head -30; grep -n 'Update\\|goDownload\\|discoverNewVersion\\|noLongerRemind' arb/intl_ru.arb; sed -n 1,50p android/app/src/main/kotlin/com/follow/clash/plugins/AppPlugin.kt; grep -n '\"[a-zA-Z]*\" ->\\|Method\\.' android/app/src/main/kotlin/com/follow/clash/plugins/AppPlugin.kt | head -30; ls lib/plugins; grep -n 'invokeMethod' lib/plugins/app.dart | head -10; grep -n 'autoCheckUpdate' -r lib/models/config.dart lib/views | head; ssh -i ~/.ssh/codex_aura_vps codex-aura@152.53.50.204 'grep -n -B2 -A2 \"android-old\\|Nexo-android\" /opt/nexo-bot/catalog.py | head -40'","description":"Read the build workflow, native plugin and strings for updates"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"1fd4ae39-09c4-4cf0-9bfe-fc8abaa281eb","hash":"63b0784c11b9f9fdbdf8be51937dd82211dd0e18f69bf75907096f80d6b4d899","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LU22GstzeZeBgomtnxmavp","type":"tool_result","content":"name: nexo-build\n\n# Builds the Nexo app for Android, macOS and Windows; started by hand from the Actions tab.\non:\n  workflow_dispatch:\n\nenv:\n  FLUTTER_VERSION: '3.47.6'\n  GO_VERSION: '1.27.1'\n  NDK_VERSION: r28c\n\njobs:\n  build:\n    name: ${{ matrix.platform }}\n    runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}\n    env:\n      HAS_KEYSTORE: ${{ secrets.KEYSTORE != '' }}\n      NEXO_MAC_UNIVERSAL: ${{ matrix.universal || '' }}\n    strategy:\n      fail-fast: false\n      matrix:\n        include:\n          - platform: android\n            os: ubuntu-latest\n          - platform: macos\n            os: macos-15-intel\n            universal: '1'\n            artifact: nexo-macos-universal\n          - platform: windows\n            os: windows-2022\n    steps:\n      - name: Checkout\n        uses: actions/checkout@v4\n        with:\n          submodules: recursive\n\n      - name: Setup Android signing\n        if: matrix.platform == 'android' && env.HAS_KEYSTORE == 'true'\n        env:\n          KEYSTORE: ${{ secrets.KEYSTORE }}\n        run: |\n          echo \"$KEYSTORE\" | base64 --decode > android/app/keystore.jks\n          {\n            echo \"keyAlias=${{ secrets.KEY_ALIAS }}\"\n            echo \"storePassword=${{ secrets.STORE_PASSWORD }}\"\n            echo \"keyPassword=${{ secrets.KEY_PASSWORD }}\"\n          } >> android/local.properties\n\n      - name: Setup Go\n        uses: actions/setup-go@v5\n        with:\n          go-version: ${{ env.GO_VERSION }}\n          cache-dependency-path: core/go.sum\n\n      - name: Setup Gradle\n        if: matrix.platform == 'android'\n        uses: gradle/actions/setup-gradle@v6\n\n      - name: Enable git long paths (Windows)\n        if: matrix.platform == 'windows'\n        run: git config --global core.longpaths true\n\n      - name: Setup Flutter\n        uses: subosito/flutter-action@v2\n        with:\n          channel: stable\n          flutter-version: ${{ env.FLUTTER_VERSION }}\n          cache: true\n\n      - name: Setup Xcode\n        if: matrix.platform == 'macos'\n        run: |\n          # newest Xcode the runner image has (macos-14 images do not ship Xcode 26)\n          latest=$(ls -d /Applications/Xcode_*.app | sort -V | tail -1)\n          sudo xcode-select -s \"$latest\"\n          xcodebuild -version\n\n      - name: Install macOS Rust targets\n        if: matrix.platform == 'macos'\n        working-directory: plugins/rust_api/rust\n        run: rustup target add aarch64-apple-darwin x86_64-apple-darwin\n\n      - name: Setup NDK\n        if: matrix.platform == 'android'\n        uses: nttld/setup-ndk@v1\n        id: build-ndk\n        with:\n          ndk-version: ${{ env.NDK_VERSION }}\n          add-to-path: true\n          link-to-sdk: true\n\n      # Build hooks see a filtered environment, so the universal switch goes through pubspec user_defines.\n      - name: Enable universal macOS core\n        if: matrix.platform == 'macos' && matrix.universal\n        run: |\n          python3 - <<'PY'\n          p = 'pubspec.yaml'\n          s = open(p).read()\n          s = s.replace('    setup:\\n      build_assets: true\\n',\n                        '    setup:\\n      build_assets: true\\n      macos_universal: true\\n', 1)\n          assert 'macos_universal: true' in s\n          open(p, 'w').write(s)\n          PY\n\n      - name: Get Flutter dependencies\n        run: flutter pub get\n\n      - name: Fetch CA certificates\n        shell: bash\n        env:\n          CA_BUNDLE: cacert-2026-09-25.pem\n          CA_BUNDLE_SHA256: a41b5d356aea97a529fe27e0f7316d2f9d946d75927476cf9cf1b90637d00505\n        run: |\n          bundle=core/Clash.Meta/component/ca/ca-certificates.crt\n          curl -fsSL --retry 3 -o \"$bundle\" \"https://curl.se/ca/$CA_BUNDLE\"\n          echo \"$CA_BUNDLE_SHA256  $bundle\" | { command -v sha256sum >/dev/null && sha256sum -c - || shasum -a 256 -c -; }\n\n      - name: Build\n        shell: bash\n        env:\n          ANDROID_NDK_HOME: ${{ steps.build-ndk.outputs.ndk-path }}\n        run: dart setup.dart ${{ matrix.platform }} --env stable -v\n\n      - name: Verify universal macOS app\n        if: matrix.platform == 'macos'\n        shell: bash\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          dmgs=(./dist/*.dmg)\n          if [ \"${#dmgs[@]}\" -ne 1 ] || [ ! -f \"${dmgs[0]}\" ]; then\n            echo 'Expected exactly one DMG in dist' >&2\n            exit 1\n          fi\n          mountpoint=$(mktemp -d)\n          mounted=0\n          cleanup() {\n            if [ \"$mounted\" -eq 1 ]; then hdiutil detach \"$mountpoint\"; fi\n            rmdir \"$mountpoint\"\n          }\n          trap cleanup EXIT\n          hdiutil attach \"${dmgs[0]}\" -readonly -nobrowse -mountpoint \"$mountpoint\"\n          mounted=1\n          app=\"$mountpoint/Nexo.app\"\n          check_slices() {\n            local binary=\"$1\" slices arch\n            slices=$(lipo -archs \"$binary\")\n            echo \"$binary: $slices\"\n            for arch in arm64 x86_64; do\n              case \" $slices \" in\n                *\" $arch \"*) ;;\n                *) echo \"Missing $arch in $binary\" >&2; return 1 ;;\n              esac\n            done\n          }\n          check_slices \"$app/Contents/MacOS/Nexo\"\n          check_slices \"$app/Contents/MacOS/FlClashCore\"\n          rust_library=$(find \"$app/Contents/Frameworks\" -path '*rust_api.framework/*' -name rust_api -type f -print -quit)\n          if [ -z \"$rust_library\" ]; then\n            echo 'Rust native asset not found in the app' >&2\n            exit 1\n          fi\n          check_slices \"$rust_library\"\n\n      - name: Upload\n        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4\n        with:\n          name: ${{ matrix.artifact || format('nexo-{0}', matrix.platform) }}\n          path: ./dist\n          retention-days: 14\nimport 'dart:io';\n\nimport 'package:package_info_plus/package_info_plus.dart';\n\nimport 'common.dart';\n\nextension PackageInfoExtension on PackageInfo {\n  String get ua => [\n    '$appName/v$version',\n    'clash-verge',\n    'Platform/${Platform.operatingSystem}',\n  ].join(' ');\n}\n\nint compareVersions(String version1, String version2) {\n  final List<String> v1 = version1.split('+')[0].split('.');\n  final List<String> v2 = version2.split('+')[0].split('.');\n  final int major1 = int.parse(v1[0]);\n  final int major2 = int.parse(v2[0]);\n  if (major1 != major2) {\n    return major1.compareTo(major2);\n  }\n  final int minor1 = v1.length > 1 ? int.parse(v1[1]) : 0;\n  final int minor2 = v2.length > 1 ? int.parse(v2[1]) : 0;\n  if (minor1 != minor2) {\n    return minor1.compareTo(minor2);\n  }\n  final int patch1 = v1.length > 2 ? int.parse(v1[2]) : 0;\n  final int patch2 = v2.length > 2 ? int.parse(v2[2]) : 0;\n  if (patch1 != patch2) {\n62:  \"autoCheckUpdate\": \"Автопроверка обновлений\",\n84:  \"autoUpdate\": \"Автообновление\",\n85:  \"autoUpdateInterval\": \"Интервал автообновления\",\n86:  \"profileAutoUpdateIntervalNullValidationDesc\": \"Введите интервал автообновления\",\n87:  \"profileAutoUpdateIntervalInvalidValidationDesc\": \"Введите корректный интервал\",\n154:  \"checkUpdate\": \"Проверить обновления\",\n155:  \"discoverNewVersion\": \"Доступна новая версия\",\n156:  \"checkUpdateError\": \"У вас уже последняя версия\",\n157:  \"goDownload\": \"Скачать\",\n169:  \"requestsAndUpdates\": \"Запросы и обновления\",\n312:  \"actionUpdateProfiles\": \"Обновить профили\",\n397:  \"fileIsUpdate\": \"Файл изменён. Сохранить изменения?\",\n398:  \"profileHasUpdate\": \"Профиль изменён. Отключить автообновление?\",\n554:  \"noLongerRemind\": \"Больше не напоминать\",\n696:  \"resourceUpdateInterval\": \"Интервал автообновления\",\n697:  \"resourceUpdateIntervalTip\": \"Интервал автообновления должен быть больше 0\",\n702:  \"geoUpdated\": \"{name}: обновлено\",\n818:  \"lastUpdated\": \"Последнее обновление\",\n938:  \"profileUpdatedAt\": \"Обновлено {time}\",\npackage com.follow.clash.plugins\n\nimport android.Manifest\nimport android.app.Activity\nimport android.app.ActivityManager\nimport android.app.AlertDialog\nimport android.content.BroadcastReceiver\nimport android.content.Context\nimport android.content.Intent\nimport android.content.IntentFilter\nimport android.content.pm.PackageManager\nimport android.net.VpnService\nimport android.os.Build\nimport android.os.Handler\nimport android.os.Looper\nimport android.os.SystemClock\nimport android.provider.Settings\nimport androidx.core.app.ActivityCompat\nimport androidx.core.content.ContextCompat\nimport androidx.core.content.ContextCompat.getSystemService\nimport androidx.core.content.pm.ShortcutInfoCompat\nimport androidx.core.content.pm.ShortcutManagerCompat\nimport androidx.core.graphics.drawable.IconCompat\nimport androidx.core.net.toUri\nimport androidx.core.view.OnApplyWindowInsetsListener\nimport androidx.core.view.ViewCompat\nimport androidx.core.view.WindowInsetsCompat\nimport com.follow.clash.R\nimport com.follow.clash.common.Components\nimport com.follow.clash.common.GlobalState\nimport com.follow.clash.common.PendingCallback\nimport com.follow.clash.common.QuickAction\nimport com.follow.clash.common.quickIntent\nimport com.follow.clash.common.registerReceiverCompat\nimport com.follow.clash.common.shortcutId\nimport com.follow.clash.getPackageIconPath\nimport com.follow.clash.packages.PackageResolver\nimport com.follow.clash.showToast\nimport com.google.gson.Gson\nimport io.flutter.embedding.engine.plugins.FlutterPlugin\nimport io.flutter.embedding.engine.plugins.activity.ActivityAware\nimport io.flutter.embedding.engine.plugins.activity.ActivityPluginBinding\nimport io.flutter.plugin.common.MethodCall\